{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children","id":626155,"title":"Sidereals and Children","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-13T19:51:49-07:00","id":626155,"title":"Sidereals and Children","content":"I don't know if the canonical material has ever addressed this, but I don't <i>think</i> it ever did. Arcane Fate blurs the memory of Sidereals in the minds of most beings governed by Fate. One has to imagine that the grim necessity of the Arcane Fate means that even a Sidereal's immediate family would be affected by it -- parents, siblings, pre-Exaltation lovers, et cetera. But how would it affect a Sidereal's children? We have to divide up these children into two categories: children produced pre-Exaltation and ones from post-Exaltation. While I can't think of any logical reason why pre-Exaltation children would be exempt from Arcane Fate, but it might be that the ones conceived after being chosen by the Maidens would be different. While the Sidereal Exaltation isn't hereditary, a fetus being exposed to said Exaltation (or more specifically, to their parent's Sidereal-resonant essence) during its formation might mean that the child produced by that Exalt &quot;dimly reflects&quot; the glory of their parent's connection to the Maidens and allows them to side-step Arcane Fate. If this is the case, would the &quot;rules&quot; be different if one parent were an Exalt and the other wasn't? Or if both parents were Sidereals? Or even more uncertain -- if one parent were a Sidereal, and the other parent were the Chosen of another?<br /> <br /> Also, if it were possible that the biological investment (or something like that) of Sidereal-resonant essence could sidestep Arcane Fate, could a Sidereal do that for some kind of construct or something even odder? I can't imagine that sex alone would be enough to bypass Arcane Fate, since if it were, the Chosen of Venus would be spending an aggravating amount of time filing paperwork with the Pattern Spiders. But a biological or overwhelmingly intimate tie with an entity -- would it be enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T20:05:55-07:00","id":626197,"title":"","content":"The god-blooded/half-caste offspring of a Sidereal who inherits a small part of their divinity is called Star-Blessed.<br /> <br /> In the 1E Player's Guide they didn't get any options to resist Arcane Fate, but I don't know about 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T20:41:02-07:00","id":626244,"title":"","content":"They would not be inherently exempt. Yes, this leads to weird results, but nothing more weird than parents who abandon their children for non-supernatural reasons.<br /> <br /> I would imagine that intentional reproduction is probably pretty rare among Sids. You know you have the potential to outlive your child by a factor of more than 100. For male Sids, you can chock it up to the cliche &quot;sowing your wild oats&quot; except it can be really reasonable to justify never having a meaningful relationship if the only people who consistently remember you are your coworkers. For women, maiden tea is pretty cheap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T20:54:07-07:00","id":626251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=626244#post626244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would not be inherently exempt. Yes, this leads to weird results, but nothing more weird than parents who abandon their children for non-supernatural reasons.<br /> <br /> I would imagine that intentional reproduction is probably pretty rare among Sids. You know you have the potential to outlive your child by a factor of more than 100. For male Sids, you can chock it up to the cliche &quot;sowing your wild oats&quot; except it can be really reasonable to justify never having a meaningful relationship if the only people who consistently remember you are your coworkers. For women, maiden tea is pretty cheap.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see where you're coming from. Considering how many children (conceived intentionally or otherwise) could be produced by a deep-cover spy with a 5,000 year lifespan, there's probably a large contingent of Creation's population with Sidereal ancestry. If all of them could easily sidestep Arcane Fate, it'd throw a monkey wrench in the plans of the Sidereals. Still, do you think the rules would be the same for a child produced by two Sidereals? Or a Sidereal and another Exalt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T20:59:47-07:00","id":626263,"title":"","content":"There's no inherent reason a Sidereal's child, even one who turned out Star-blessed or who was the product of two Sidereals or both, would be different from any other mortals for Arcane Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T21:10:09-07:00","id":626277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=626263#post626263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no inherent reason a Sidereal's child, even one who turned out Star-blessed or who was the product of two Sidereals or both, would be different from any other mortals for Arcane Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't think so? It strikes me as something of a strange situation when I consider the child of two Sidereals. Presumably, this child would be living in Yu-Shan, all things being equal. Would nobody be raising questions about a human child living by themselves in Heaven? Would this child be unable to clearly remember their parents? Going to the extremes, would that mean that nanny-gods hired by the Sidereal parents would be unable to remember being hired to take care of this human child just sort of living alone in Yu-Shan?<br /> <br /> It just seems ... odd for the child of two Sidereals to be under the effects of Arcane Fate. To my mind, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T21:36:00-07:00","id":626296,"title":"","content":"Don't mortals exposed to a Sidereal repeatedly develop a sort of resistance as reflected by the Acquaintances background? I imagine children have more than enough exposure to their Sidereal mother to count for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T00:36:34-07:00","id":626406,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Yes. Page 119 of MoEP:Sidereals, advises that: &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000ff\">A character\u2019s Familiars and Acquaintances are immune, as are all Sidereals, all officials and functionaries of the Bureau of Destiny, all Celestial </span><span style=\"color:#0000ff\">gods, and any creatures outside of fate.</span>&quot;<br /> <br /> So if a sidereal <i>invests </i>time raising a family they'd remember, but not so much if they practice absentee parenting. Of course, even if close</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">family and neighbours remember the sidereal parent, there would still be problems with distant family and such.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 08-14-2015, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T01:10:48-07:00","id":626422,"title":"","content":"There's also the issue that Acquaintance isn't perfect. An Acquaintance will remember the Sidereal, vaguely. Even the Sidereal's lovers won't really think about her when she's not there.<br /> <br /> Essentially, breaking the masque sucked for the Sidereals, it made it extremely difficult for them to make friends with humans. They're just stuck with other Sidereals, and Celestial Gods. Is it any wonder they became arrogant, disconnected from humanity, puppet masters behind the scenes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T02:17:11-07:00","id":626439,"title":"","content":"Now to think of which Contellations make for good resplendencies for a parent (which the Sidereal can easily align with their actual identity and appearance, since there are other conditions to assigning it a disguise). <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how many children (conceived intentionally or otherwise) could be produced by a deep-cover spy with a 5,000 year lifespan</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe be responsible enough to invest in some decent contraceptives. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">there's probably a large contingent of Creation's population with Sidereal ancestry</div> </div> </div> </div> It's not really fitting to the intended image, so not really. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If all of them could easily sidestep Arcane Fate, it'd throw a monkey wrench in the plans of the Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div> On the other hand, if you <i>did</i> follow the idea of large numbers of Sidereal descendents... actually, no, it still wouldn't prove anything, Half-Caste status is basically never transferable. Whatever benefits your one or two children get, your innumerable great-great-great grandchildren will not have it at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T02:52:53-07:00","id":626460,"title":"","content":"That chapter fiction in 1e Sidereals where Shepherd of the North Star is returning from a steamy night with his celestial goddess lover was quite striking to me, and therefore I like the idea that Sidereals have most of their romantic engagements with the divine. It seems fitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T05:51:08-07:00","id":626522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=626460#post626460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That chapter fiction in 1e Sidereals where Shepherd of the North Star is returning from a steamy night with his celestial goddess lover was quite striking to me, and therefore I like the idea that Sidereals have most of their romantic engagements with the divine. It seems fitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I did in Hero. The majority of the children from these Sidereal-Divine relationships ending working in the Bureau of Destiny in some way. A child of a Sidereal is not immune to Arcane Fate, so there is some fancy paperwork done at times to employ a toddler in the Bureau. As an adult, they end up continuing to work in the Bureau (or else Arcane Fate will slowly erode memories of their parent). One Sidereal jokes that he bred his own secretary. <br /> <br /> But there are two things I hope 3rd Edition clears up:<br /> <br /> 1 - Guidelines on how a Sidereal can acquire Acquaintances. How long does it take? How often does a Sidereal need to interact with a person to have them become an Acquaintance? Is there any maintenance? Do they need the Ride charms to do it? <br /> <br /> 2 \u2013 Why are gods in the Bureau of Destiny, the Celestial Lions, and the Auditors in Yu-Shan immune to Arcane Fate? Does it have to do with a God\u2019s Domain? Or some weird Bureaucratic Shenanigans? The Maidens said so? I have any employee in Bureau of Destiny immune to Arcane Fate, but that might not be true. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T06:08:48-07:00","id":626535,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that, mechanically, it isn't that hard to beat Arcane Fate in either edition. A Sidereal who uses astrology on their kinfolk to make it easier (or is that explicitly banned?) or simply develops a training regimen for them so they have &quot;Remembering Sidereals +3&quot; as the relevant specialty could have family members who basically remember them fully and permanently without to much effort.<br /> <br /> That's the mechanical overlay, of course. In-universe, that would be represented by the Sidereal anchoring themselves to their loved ones solidly, combined with them blessing their relationships with the power of the stars, in order to prevent their blood kin from drifting away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T06:14:06-07:00","id":626540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=626251#post626251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see where you're coming from. Considering how many children (conceived intentionally or otherwise) could be produced by a deep-cover spy with a 5,000 year lifespan, there's probably a large contingent of Creation's population with Sidereal ancestry. If all of them could easily sidestep Arcane Fate, it'd throw a monkey wrench in the plans of the Sidereals. Still, do you think the rules would be the same for a child produced by two Sidereals? Or a Sidereal and another Exalt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I don't think the rules are necessarily going to be the same for two children produced by the same couple.<br /> One child might remember the infrequent visits of their Sidereal mother while the other thinks they're making excuses for their absent parent or have too much imagination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T06:24:48-07:00","id":626550,"title":"","content":"Being able to see through your parent's Arcane Fate strikes me as a reasonable minor thing for a Sidereal's Half-Caste to have.<br /> <br /> Pre-Exaltation children probably do not have any special benefit, unless it's just really fucking depressing at the table, in which case sure, they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T07:21:07-07:00","id":626606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=626550#post626550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being able to see through your parent's Arcane Fate strikes me as a reasonable minor thing for a Sidereal's Half-Caste to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tangent: I know that Half-Castes in general were problematic in a bunch of ways, but I goddamn loved Sidereal Half-Castes. They could have access to a surprisingly wide swathe of the Sidereal charmset (owing to the Sidereals not relying on perfects or persistents a lot, which is what the Half-Caste mechanical rules seemed more focused than anything else on preventing access to) which makes them pretty effective agents of the Bureau in their own right even without access to astrology, and I just really love the idea that of course there are a ton of half-divine, half-Sidereal offspring living and working in Yu-Shan, because the Sidereals don't stop being human just because they're Sidereals, and they're going to fall in love with and start families within the society they live in, and that society is mostly &quot;other gods&quot; and &quot;other Sidereals.&quot;<br /> <br /> I've run mostly Sidereal games and often toss in &quot;oh, sure, at any given time there's a couple score of these guys around. Some of them moved on to become gods, a few of them have the Longevity or Immortality pox and have been working for the Bureau for a long time, but for the most part they're just the kids of the Sidereals. They train in their powerset and bitch about their parents and get into trouble and spy on each other and occasionally save the world, just like their parents do.&quot; It gives me more &quot;bodies&quot; to work with; I can't expand the Five-Score Fellowship directly, after all.<br /> <br /> Best use I ever made of one was when I made her the PCs boss, because she was older than them and had longer chops with the Bureau. One of my PC's fucking hated that their Exalted could be bossed around by some Half-Caste purely because she was older, wiser, and really good at her job. (This guy wasn't a problem player by any means but he had a really huge sense of &quot;Exalted rule, others obey&quot; when it came to the setting.) It caused him no end of trouble and made a real interesting story.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T07:44:00-07:00","id":626631,"title":"","content":"I prefer Star Blessed to have a different relationship with fate to their Sidereal parents.<br /> <br /> To me, if the Sidereals are &quot;puppeteers&quot; who orchestrate what\u2019s supposed to happen then the Star Blessed are unusually self-aware puppets. They don\u2019t sit in on fate planning meetings (or at least they're not supposed to) but they can feel the tugging of their own thread at times and use that to their advantage. I portray them with a Destiny (in the 2e background sense) that they're capable of whole heartedly embracing or tweaking in subtle ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 08-14-2015, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T08:01:51-07:00","id":626645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=626606#post626606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tangent: I know that Half-Castes in general were problematic in a bunch of ways, but I goddamn loved Sidereal Half-Castes. They could have access to a surprisingly wide swathe of the Sidereal charmset (owing to the Sidereals not relying on perfects or persistents a lot, which is what the Half-Caste mechanical rules seemed more focused than anything else on preventing access to) which makes them pretty effective agents of the Bureau in their own right even without access to astrology, and I just really love the idea that of course there are a ton of half-divine, half-Sidereal offspring living and working in Yu-Shan, because the Sidereals don't stop being human just because they're Sidereals, and they're going to fall in love with and start families within the society they live in, and that society is mostly &quot;other gods&quot; and &quot;other Sidereals.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of steps all over the Sidereal image of being overworked and needing to keep a handle on so much that it significantly damages the viability of Sidereal Half-Castes working anything like that.<br /> <br /> I mean, even if somebody doesn't really care for the idea of overworked Sidereals at all, the image of them cultivating large families in order to create a kind of indentured work force... it doesn't really fit the heavenly sage/secret mastermind image.<br /> <br /> I think it can be just about salvaged with the idea that when some random person needs to be selected to fulfill some destined role, children or other close descendants of Sidereals might be disproportionately represented, but other than that...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">unless it's just really fucking depressing at the table, in which case sure, they can.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Hey! Who's giving you permission to make the Sidereal work and experience non-depressing? I have a sternly worded letter with their name on it.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T08:44:26-07:00","id":626689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=626439#post626439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Maybe be responsible enough to invest in some decent contraceptives. It's not really fitting to the intended image, so not really.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I have to disagree. I think the idea of Sidereals in Resplendent Destinies conceiving children to be absolutely in-line with their image. When I think of the Sidereals, the group I use as personal inspiration is the Bene Gesserit of <i>Dune</i>. And for the Bene Gesserit, children created by their members were a major part of their political plans -- a child could be easily used as a pawn in their schemes, and even the untalented and extraneous children could be worked into some kind of position where they were useful. While the Bene Gesserit had a long-term goal different than the Sidereals, it was clear from <i>Dune</i> that in the short term, on a practical level, the Bene Gesserit were cultivating lines of aristocrat children to create an environment in which they could do their business easier, or to have leaders more sympathetic to their plans.<br /> <br /> I could see a Chosen of Serenity or Endings creating a Resplendent Destiny as a wife for a powerful tyrant, and giving birth to the tyrant's child in order to have somebody on the throne for stability's sake after the Sidereal poisons the child's father. That the child would also be tied to the Sidereal in a magical way would no doubt be a plus for her plans. A callous Sidereal would probably be apt to create children for the sake of an assignment and discard them afterwards like a coat to be taken off; but I think it would be interesting for a more compassionate Sidereal to feel a twinge of guilt about the children they needed to conceive and then abandon. I could definitely see a Sidereal like that keeping tabs on their mortal children's lives and maybe nudging fate every once in a while as an invisible gift for those children.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Originally posted by <b>Robert Vance</b><br /> Being able to see through your parent's Arcane Fate strikes me as a reasonable minor thing for a Sidereal's Half-Caste to have.<br /> <br /> Pre-Exaltation children probably do not have any special benefit, unless it's just really fucking depressing at the table, in which case sure, they can. </div> </div> </div>See, that's what I was thinking. I imagine that nine times out of ten, the mortal children of Celestial Exalts aren't even as powerful (for multiple definitions of that word) as a God-Blooded child. But given that the Exaltation is such a magical, irrepressible force, it would seem out-of-place for a child being bathed in their parent or parents' Exalted essence during conception to not resonate with that essence in some way. The child of an Abyssal father might not be a cackling necromancer covered in Soulsteel, but maybe the child grows up with pale hair and an unquenchable desire to join the Immaculate Order as a monk specializing in exorcism. The child of a Solar mother might not be a glorious demigod who can perform the General of the All-Seeing Sun charm, but maybe the child finds it easy to become chieftain of their tribe of barbarians and becomes celebrated in local stories for their exploits in uniting the tribes.<br /> <br /> The child of two Sidereals might be able to see past Arcane Fate thanks to the overwhelming resonance of their parents' Exaltations in their soul (and the Bureau of Destiny prefers to keep them in Yu-Shan for the sake of keeping a close eye on them for that reason).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","user":"Kallipolis","date":". 08-14-2015, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T09:00:39-07:00","id":626699,"title":"","content":"Also, if I had to go the route of giving Star Blessed actual Sidereal powers (like say if I was writing this for an actual book and the evils of word count meant I couldn\u2019t write a list of charms or merits) I\u2019d give them Astrology.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s something Sidereals don\u2019t use often enough and has a long history of being weak and overpriced but could be really potent in the hands of an otherwise mortal mastermind who could construct elaborate false personas and tweak odds in their favour if they had the necessary prep time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T09:14:49-07:00","id":626705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=626645#post626645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This kind of steps all over the Sidereal image of being overworked and needing to keep a handle on so much that it significantly damages the viability of Sidereal Half-Castes working anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even overworked people have families and make time for them, tho, don't they? I mean, the Sidereals have enough time for personal projects, especially if they're not involved in factional politics, which are an enormous part of their workload. It's not like they're chained to their desks, they do go home every evening and they have time to go on vacation and enjoy their salaries.<br /> <br /> Now, they might be the kind of distant workaholic parents who never make it to their kids recitals and need their secretaries to remind them of their birthdays, but that's a different thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, even if somebody doesn't really care for the idea of overworked Sidereals at all, the image of them cultivating large families in order to create a kind of indentured work force... it doesn't really fit the heavenly sage/secret mastermind image. </div> </div> </div>... whoa, what?<br /> <br /> How on earth did you get from what I said to &quot;Sidereals cultivate large families in order to create a kind of indentured work force?&quot; Because you're right, that would be insane and completely destroy a lot of their themes.<br /> <br /> The way I've run it is utilizing this logic chain: Sidereals, at least those who are interested, probably cultivate families because they're human and cultivating families is what people do, and their kids probably associate with each other because when you're kids you meet the kids of your parents friends and co-workers a lot, and a number of them probably end up working for the Celestial Bureaucracy in some capacity because they have access to a bunch of Sidereal Charms and that makes them deeply employable to the Bureau of Destiny in particular and the Celestial Bureacracy in general, and if you grew up in a neighborhood in Yu-Shan it was probably expected this is what you'd do someday. (Certainly, there would be exceptions.) There would never be a giant army of them, but between twenty to forty Half-Castes at any given time always felt about right to me. They hang out with each other and with God-Blooded and do their jobs and live their lives and have deeply complicated relationships with their parents. Some of them are quite puissant, the children of dalliances between elder Sidereals and potent Gods who are very nearly deities in their own right; others are basically humans with a few neat tricks but never really got the knack of their Charmset.<br /> <br /> It doesn't<i> have to be </i>like that. But I love the idea, I find it in-theme, and I find it useful, so I've often made it like that. I am, certainly, open to arguments that I've made a terrible mistake; indeed, I've had to have players talk me down from what I thought were awful ideas a number of times. But it seems like you had a completely erroneous idea of what I was saying.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T11:21:05-07:00","id":626753,"title":"","content":"I think I'd prefer the Essence requirements of non-Excellency charms to be one higher for half-castes. So there are Star-Blessed who have very minor heritage powers or can penetrate Arcane Fate somewhat and tweak their own destinies slightly, but are basically mortal and not qualified for almost any work in Yu-Shan. There are some Star-Blessed who enlighten their essence and learn very basic Sidereal charms -- they're less useful than many gods, but have some use. Then there are a small number who raise their Essence to 3, who can learn more charms and be more useful as minor functionaries and agents of the Bureaus. They may be useful as agents of their parents, because they don't have an Arcane Fate, so they can more easily cultivate and maintain networks of informants, property, and holdings on behalf of their parents.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: But their usefulness to their parents is proportional to the time said parent spends cultivating a relationship with them, vs. just handing them off to a nanny. And those children are probably inconvenient as kids, and sometimes politically inconvenient as adults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-14-2015, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T13:59:08-07:00","id":626952,"title":"","content":"Is anyone else getting visions of the Google-Spider Secretary being stuck in the office with the Sid's kid while the parent is out on an errand, growing to like the kid, and occasionally delivering those terrible finger paint creations instead of actual information?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:29:06-07:00","id":626974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for the Bene Gesserit, children created by their members were a major part of their political plans -- a child could be easily used as a pawn in their schemes, and even the untalented and extraneous children could be worked into some kind of position where they were useful.</div> </div> </div> </div> That works quite fine for that other fictional property. It's not what the Sidereals are. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see a Chosen of Serenity or Endings creating a Resplendent Destiny as a wife for a powerful tyrant, and giving birth to the tyrant's child in order to have somebody on the throne for stability's sake after the Sidereal poisons the child's father.</div> </div> </div> </div> And nobody else can do that? The Bene Gesserit do their thing because <i>their own</i> genetics are pertinant to the people they're producing. If the only thing you need is to make sure a ruler has an heir, there are dozens of things that the Sidereal can do that are more sensible than carrying the child themselves. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How on earth did you get from what I said to &quot;Sidereals cultivate large families in order to create a kind of indentured work force?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I started from here <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just really love the idea that of course there are a ton of half-divine, half-Sidereal offspring living and working in Yu-Shan</div> </div> </div> </div> And then stopped right there because it pretty much covers the whole thing. The Sidereals are not making their lives and jobs easier by having lots of children. If their powers are significant to doing what Sidereals do, then virtually nobody else has the powers of a Sidereal. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am, certainly, open to arguments that I've made a terrible mistake</div> </div> </div> </div> Your own games are your own business, but the books should maintain a certain consistency. It's in about the same boat as how nobody has bought the rarity of starmetal for a long time, because they all think in terms of just killing gods en masse for it, and the books actively contradicted themselves by presenting that image as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:52:17-07:00","id":626989,"title":"","content":"I can definitely see Sidereals manipulating and breeding bloodlines of mortals, and at least influencing the breeding of Dragon-Blooded. But they will not frequently have a reason to add their own blood to the mix, and if they do it will probably be a man doing it, so it's less inconvenient.<br /> <br /> However, the characteristics they could and would &quot;breed&quot; in mortals mostly would be the manipulation of the culture and education of a family, and the sort of destinies that tie to a bloodline, because the quasi-magical powers that Bene Gesserit cultivate just don't run in mortal families in Creation. Even spirits' blood and Celestial blood only last a few generations at most before petering out, unless you start a family of beastmen -- which are out of theme for Sidereals and probably no use to them.<br /> <br /> It's tempting to imagine more callous or desperate Sidereals creating Star-Blessed puppets, the same way so many corrupt gods create and use god-blooded. But Gods ensure the usefulness of their god-blooded puppets by personally raising and molding them to be and do what they want. Sidereals don't have the time to do that with their children. Conversely, they have other options for using and exploiting people they aren't related to -- including tricking someone into thinking they're related.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-14-2015, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T15:11:12-07:00","id":627011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=626974#post626974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That works quite fine for that other fictional property. It's not what the Sidereals are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's so absurd to draw parallels between one fictional universe and another, particularly when the Exalted sourcebook gives big lists of other works which can be cribbed for inspiration. I think that the Sidereals <i>are</i> the Bene Gesserit, some elements aside. I mean, both groups are uncanny masters of martial arts; both groups never touch thrones themselves, but act as viziers and kingmakers for those who do; both groups are invisible in their true form all but the most knowledgeable, and are tolerated only because they've made themselves indispensable to the aristocracy; and both groups' members craft identities that are so intricate that agents can run the risk of going native (read: Lady Jessica). Even the Missionaria Protectiva is pretty similar to the Immaculate faith in terms of being a religious manipulation done for the sake of the plots of the powers-that-be. I still think that the Bene Gesserit represent a great source of inspiration for the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And nobody else can do that? The Bene Gesserit do their thing because <i>their own</i> genetics are pertinant to the people they're producing. If the only thing you need is to make sure a ruler has an heir, there are dozens of things that the Sidereal can do that are more sensible than carrying the child themselves. </div> </div> </div>Even setting aside the Bene Gesserit, it's a fact in human history that children make for exceptional social and political tools. Acting as the regent of a child monarch means that they grow up with a will that is pliant to your wishes -- and even more so when that child is your own, as evinced by queen-mothers such as Catherine de' Medici. Impregnating or being impregnated by a person of higher status has been a method people have used for millennia to climb the social ranks. Having a child with a person creates ties of trust between the parents -- something that can, and likely has, been manipulated before by one party looking for some kind of gain. Creating a child creates a clear line of succession for monarchs and aristocrats. Having many children has historically been seen as a direct corollary of one's wealth, status, and prestige -- the &quot;war of pregnancies&quot; between Leah and Rachel in the Tanach, and between Kaushalya, Sumitra, and Kaikeyi in the Ramayana, were methods by which those aristocratic women jockeyed for status in their society.<br /> <br /> Considering that the Sidereals need to remain undercover when working in Creation, one has to imagine that they reserve their supernatural powers for situations that genuinely require them. And if having a child is the simplest or most effective natural way of insinuating into or manipulating a social structure, why would a Sidereal trust that task to someone else? Especially when their own child would prove so much easier a variable to control?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T15:21:27-07:00","id":627044,"title":"","content":"Well, Half-Castes do not exist in my games, but if I were forced to use them somehow, I'd want them to have access to exactly zero Exalted Charms.<br /> <br /> As for Sidereals and having children, some might employ contraceptives, others enjoy having bunches of kids over the millennia and some have kids sporadically, and their interest in offspring can certainly change in various periods within their long lives. I don't really see how one could say all Sidereals (or nearly enough to all) would fit the same mold regarding their interest in children and family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T16:09:17-07:00","id":627087,"title":"","content":"There were ways around it, in the games I'd been in. For starters, if both of the parents were Sidereals, then the child would remember them as well as any, provided they weren't left in a wicker basket on somebody else's doorstep (babies get in the way of paperwork and other responsibilities to Yu Shan's bureaucracy, after all). Those children conceived, and brought to term, while a Sidereal in a Astrological Fate (either gender works, so even the non-birthing one, so long as they stay close to the child-to-be and maintain 'deep cover') are typically remembered based on the personality and prowesses of that sign (which mkes things interesting for those conceived and raised under the sign of the Gull). Children of Sidereals and other Essence-high persons remember only a vague two-to-three bullet list of adjectives around a shadowy visage.... and a strange fascination with spiders. Everyone else is just out of luck.<br /> <br /> To be fair, the only long-lasting Starblessed was a girl who ended up becoming the spitting image of the Resistance resplendence... which suited the Sidereal just fine, as he treated her like a foot-on-the-ground mook, kept alive but not fully in the loop, essentially using her like a (valueble) pawn. Sidereals, am I right?<br /> <br /> ... who am i kidding, most Exalted types might do the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T16:26:40-07:00","id":627100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=626540#post626540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I don't think the rules are necessarily going to be the same for two children produced by the same couple.<br /> One child might remember the infrequent visits of their Sidereal mother while the other thinks they're making excuses for their absent parent or have too much imagination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, that kind of opens up the interesting idea of your imaginary friend actually being your Sidereal parent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T16:45:02-07:00","id":627113,"title":"","content":"Now, while everyone is busy discussing Sidereals, their children,and contraception, I want to remind everyone that a... liberal reading of &quot;Someone Else's Destiny&quot; allows Sidereals to punch their pregnancies into other people, and that they're <i>definitely</i> able to just dodge pregnancy. After all, they're the only ones who are allowed to dodge falling damage without also dodging the ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T17:41:55-07:00","id":627134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=626974#post626974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, I started from here And then stopped right there because it pretty much covers the whole thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>... maybe you could actually read my posts before responding to them, then, instead of just stopping the second you see something that seems problematic? I mean, that's what I do with yours. It seems only courteous. I still don't know where you got &quot;the Sidereals deliberately breed to create indentured servants&quot; from in my statements, but I can say that perhaps if you'd read what I wrote, the more logical conclusion would have been &quot;oh, he perhaps overstated things when he used the word 'ton'.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T18:39:14-07:00","id":627160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=627011#post627011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's so absurd to draw parallels between one fictional universe and another, particularly when the Exalted sourcebook gives big lists of other works which can be cribbed for inspiration. I think that the Sidereals <i>are</i> the Bene Gesserit, some elements aside. I mean, both groups are uncanny masters of martial arts; both groups never touch thrones themselves, but act as viziers and kingmakers for those who do; both groups are invisible in their true form all but the most knowledgeable, and are tolerated only because they've made themselves indispensable to the aristocracy; and both groups' members craft identities that are so intricate that agents can run the risk of going native (read: Lady Jessica). Even the Missionaria Protectiva is pretty similar to the Immaculate faith in terms of being a religious manipulation done for the sake of the plots of the powers-that-be. I still think that the Bene Gesserit represent a great source of inspiration for the Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Half of these parallels are not accurate.<br /> <br /> And there are entirely different reasons for Sidereals not ruling vs Bene Gesserit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T18:53:37-07:00","id":627169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=627160#post627160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Half of these parallels are not accurate.<br /> <br /> And there are entirely different reasons for Sidereals not ruling vs Bene Gesserit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree? From my perspective, I don't know how you can't see the parallels between the Sidereals and the Bene Gesserit, so I think there's a great deal of subjectivity in the comparison. I mean, yes, there are differences because <i>Dune</i> is <i>Dune</i> and Exalted is Exalted. But do tell -- why didn't you think those parallels were apt?<br /> <br /> (Although I do think it's interesting to compare the Bene Gesserit to the Sidereals in that one group has a particular goal that acts as an intriguing mirror to the other's. The Bene Gesserit shepherd humanity in order to produce a god. The Sidereals shepherd humanity to prevent the return of gods.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T18:54:36-07:00","id":627170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think that the Bene Gesserit represent a great source of inspiration for the Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div> Certainly they are. The mistake is in assuming that being an inspiration means replicating details thoughtlessly. For example, the Sidereal Exalted include men. That is a not insigificant detail, since the Bene Gesserit was designed with all kinds of internal justifications, both in practice and made up science/spiritualism, for why they were all women.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T21:20:43-07:00","id":627222,"title":"","content":"Oh god, now I'm like 99% certain that Anys Syn is trying to get Ragara Myrun to achieve the Blossom of the Perfected Lotus because it will make him the Kwisatz Haderach.<br /> <br /> I'm never going to NOT be able to think that about him now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T21:27:19-07:00","id":627226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=627222#post627222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh god, now I'm like 99% certain that Anys Syn is trying to get Ragara Myrun to achieve the Blossom of the Perfected Lotus because it will make him the Kwisatz Haderach.<br /> <br /> I'm never going to NOT be able to think that about him now.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sleeper has awoken!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T00:36:28-07:00","id":627356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=627160#post627160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Half of these parallels are not accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=627169#post627169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Both groups are uncanny masters of martial arts&quot; - True<br /> &quot;Both groups never touch thrones themselves, but act as viziers and kingmakers for those who do&quot; - Technically true, but the BG do so because they consider it the most efficient way (and because they consider themselves above petty politics), the Sidereals do so because they <i>can't</i> do it any other way (the risks to them when exposed would be to high if they placed themselves on the throne).<br /> &quot;Both groups are invisible in their true form all but the most knowledgeable&quot; - Huh? The BG were invisible? I got the impression that their existance was rather well-known, it was their <i>abilities</i> that were shrouded in mystery. (To a lesser extend, also their agents and goals, but that was just regular Dune politics. <i>Everyone</i> had hidden agents and goals.)<br /> &quot;Are tolerated only because they've made themselves indispensable to the aristocracy&quot; - Well, the Scarlet Empress tollerated the Sidereals because she couldn't fight them anyway, and because she's to pragmatic to show a gift horse in the mouth. It's similar, but not on the same - the aristrocrats in the Dune universe don't have a standing &quot;kill on sight&quot; order against the BG that's only ignored by the higher ups. Most Dragon-Blooded in Creation, however, still consider Sidereals regular Anathema. Also, the BG worked themselves up into a position where they might be a threat, and have to keep people from disposing of them - Sids arguably worked themselves <i>down</i> into a position where people might be able to dispose of them.<br /> &quot;Both groups' members craft identities that are so intricate that agents can run the risk of going native (read: Lady Jessica).&quot; - Wait, was that ever suggested to be a Sidereal thing, except for the Green Lady? That seemed more to be a one-character plothook, less a general Sidereal thing.<br /> &quot;Even the Missionaria Protectiva is pretty similar to the Immaculate faith in terms of being a religious manipulation done for the sake of the plots of the powers-that-be.&quot; - IIRC, it was mostly done for the direct sake of the BG themselves, to manipulate existing power systems for their benefit - but the Sids knowingly knowingly created a power system from scratch and placed themselves in the villain role in the IF, to make it harder for other Celestials to talk themselves out of it.<br /> &quot;I still think that the Bene Gesserit represent a great source of inspiration for the Sidereals.&quot; - To some degree, sure. The fact that there are so many similarities (even if these similarities end up being different when examined closer) shows they can be used as an inspiration. But they're not really the same.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=627169#post627169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Although I do think it's interesting to compare the Bene Gesserit to the Sidereals in that one group has a particular goal that acts as an intriguing mirror to the other's. The Bene Gesserit shepherd humanity in order to produce a god. The Sidereals shepherd humanity to prevent the return of gods.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to go with &quot;Nnnnnnnno&quot;.<br /> The BG try (and succeed) to create a being &quot;larger than human&quot;. The Sids did dispose of &quot;larger than human&quot; beings and try to prevent their return, but their shepherding of humanity is (or rather, was) independant of this - they just want to save the world, and consider these &quot;larger than human&quot; beings <i>one</i> of the threats to the world. But in the end, shepherding humanity is its own purpose, that's just co-opted out of necessity to fight other threats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T01:40:04-07:00","id":627369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=627356#post627356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Both groups never touch thrones themselves, but act as viziers and kingmakers for those who do&quot; - Technically true, but the BG do so because they consider it the most efficient way (and because they consider themselves above petty politics), the Sidereals do so because they <i>can't</i> do it any other way (the risks to them when exposed would be to high if they placed themselves on the throne).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't disagree. There's actually a magical enforcement on the Sidereals' behavior, but both the Bene Gesserit and the Sidereals end up playing the trope of the &quot;evil vizier&quot; regardless of the specifics behind their stories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Both groups are invisible in their true form all but the most knowledgeable&quot; - Huh? The BG were invisible? I got the impression that their existance was rather well-known, it was their <i>abilities</i> that were shrouded in mystery. (To a lesser extend, also their agents and goals, but that was just regular Dune politics. <i>Everyone</i> had hidden agents and goals.) </div> </div> </div>Admittedly, it's been a long time since I've read <i>Dune</i>, but from what I recall, the Bene Gesserit were not an organization well-understood by non-aristocrats. The sisters of the order only seemed to join aristocratic households one or two at a time, meaning that the average person on the street -- if they even knew about the Bene Gesserit at all -- would have considered them strange and alien &quot;witches&quot; best avoided. In metaphorical terms, they were &quot;invisible&quot; to everybody but the upper 1% of society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Are tolerated only because they've made themselves indispensable to the aristocracy&quot; - Well, the Scarlet Empress tollerated the Sidereals because she couldn't fight them anyway, and because she's to pragmatic to show a gift horse in the mouth. It's similar, but not on the same - the aristrocrats in the Dune universe don't have a standing &quot;kill on sight&quot; order against the BG that's only ignored by the higher ups. Most Dragon-Blooded in Creation, however, still consider Sidereals regular Anathema. Also, the BG worked themselves up into a position where they might be a threat, and have to keep people from disposing of them - Sids arguably worked themselves <i>down</i> into a position where people might be able to dispose of them. </div> </div> </div>You're right, but I was focusing on the &quot;made themselves indispensable&quot; aspect that both the Sidereals and Bene Gesserit share. The Dragon-Blooded who know about the Sidereals are generally not well-disposed towards them. Mnemon doesn't particularly like them. And no doubt the Scarlet Empress didn't like them. Certainly if the Realm had consolidated its efforts, it could have seriously harmed the ability of the Sidereals to work in Creation. But the Realm didn't, because the knowledgeable Dragon-Blooded realized that incredibly powerful spies with the power to manipulate destiny were better to have on their sides than not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Both groups' members craft identities that are so intricate that agents can run the risk of going native (read: Lady Jessica).&quot; - Wait, was that ever suggested to be a Sidereal thing, except for the Green Lady? That seemed more to be a one-character plothook, less a general Sidereal thing. </div> </div> </div>I think that it's a common thing among Sidereals that the radical changes in Creation are causing them to reevaluate the standard Sidereal party line. Being exposed to the incursions of Lunar contra-civilizations, the advent of the Abyssals and Infernals, and -- most importantly -- the return of a Solar alternative to the Realm, is making Sidereals question their role in Creation.<br /> <br /> But more specifically, one of the themes of the Sidereals is that Arcane Fate isolates them so much from humanity that their Resplendent Destinies often represent a desperate attempt to connect to the people they meet during their assignments. If a Sidereal goes Ronin (or goes Lady Jessica in this case), one has to imagine that many times that choice results from the renegade choosing to preserve something in Creation they were ordered to alter or destroy by Yu-Shan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Even the Missionaria Protectiva is pretty similar to the Immaculate faith in terms of being a religious manipulation done for the sake of the plots of the powers-that-be.&quot; - IIRC, it was mostly done for the direct sake of the BG themselves, to manipulate existing power systems for their benefit - but the Sids knowingly knowingly created a power system from scratch and placed themselves in the villain role in the IF, to make it harder for other Celestials to talk themselves out of it. </div> </div> </div>The Immaculate Faith had to be set up the way it was, or people would start asking questions about the role the Sidereals played in its creation, and potentially unravel their role in the Usurpation. But still, the Immaculate Faith is also set up that a Sidereal who takes precautions is extremely unlikely to be targeted by Realm hostility. The small chance of an unprepared Sidereal being caught flatfooted by Immaculate faithful is greatly outweighed by the usefulness of having nearly all of Creation as a weapon to turn against the Solars, Lunars, and other enemies of Creation. And while the Immaculate Faith may have been created <i>ex nihilo</i>, the Missionaria Protectiva also represented exploitable tropes being created out of wholecloth and inserted in various worlds' myths for the Bene Gesserit's sake.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The BG try (and succeed) to create a being &quot;larger than human&quot;. The Sids did dispose of &quot;larger than human&quot; beings and try to prevent their return, but their shepherding of humanity is (or rather, was) independant of this - they just want to save the world, and consider these &quot;larger than human&quot; beings <i>one</i> of the threats to the world. But in the end, shepherding humanity is its own purpose, that's just co-opted out of necessity to fight other threats. </div> </div> </div>I was being a little tongue-in-cheek about this one, but if I recall correctly, the Bene Gesserit were attempting to produce the Kwisatz Haderach in an attempt to transcend the limitations of humanity that led to people being enslaved by artificial intelligences and by the inherent weaknesses that caused the stagnation of the Old Empire. In this way, the Bene Gesserit were indeed attempting to &quot;save the world&quot; from threats both external and internal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T02:57:04-07:00","id":627417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=627369#post627369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly, it's been a long time since I've read <i>Dune</i>, but from what I recall, the Bene Gesserit were not an organization well-understood by non-aristocrats. The sisters of the order only seemed to join aristocratic households one or two at a time, meaning that the average person on the street -- if they even knew about the Bene Gesserit at all -- would have considered them strange and alien &quot;witches&quot; best avoided. In metaphorical terms, they were &quot;invisible&quot; to everybody but the upper 1% of society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Poorly understood sure, but they didn't make their existence a secret. People knew about the &quot;Bene Gesserit Witches&quot; as much as they knew about the Navigators or the Bene Tleilax or the Ixians - people didn't know what they wanted or how they did things (even Aristrocrats only had a rudimentary understanding of these parts), and they shrouded themselves in myths, but people knew they were a thing - to the degree that people knew that the words of a &quot;Witch&quot; could control you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=627369#post627369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it's a common thing among Sidereals that the radical changes in Creation are causing them to reevaluate the standard Sidereal party line. Being exposed to the incursions of Lunar contra-civilizations, the advent of the Abyssals and Infernals, and -- most importantly -- the return of a Solar alternative to the Realm, is making Sidereals question their role in Creation.<br /> <br /> But more specifically, one of the themes of the Sidereals is that Arcane Fate isolates them so much from humanity that their Resplendent Destinies often represent a desperate attempt to connect to the people they meet during their assignments. If a Sidereal goes Ronin (or goes Lady Jessica in this case), one has to imagine that many times that choice results from the renegade choosing to preserve something in Creation they were ordered to alter or destroy by Yu-Shan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that Lady Jessica's &quot;betrayal&quot; is portrayed as an exceptionally rare thing - the BG are actually surprised it happened, and it's noted that the reason she later concieved Paul's sister was an attempt to <i>still</i> follow her original order (&quot;give birth to a daughter that could be married to the Harkonen for a high chance to produce a [I'm not even trying to spell that]&quot;). Also, at least in the core line (I'm not familiar with the prequels and such other authors later added to the line), there are never other factions that peaque the BG's interests - when the Empire ends, the BGs are pretty much shocked, and only &quot;accept&quot; Paul because, well, he just conquered the galaxy, and they're to pragmatic to fight a battle they can't win.<br /> <br /> Also, their goals change:<br /> From &quot;Create a [I'm not even trying to spell that]&quot; to &quot;Prevent the raise of a new [I'm not even trying to spell that] (also, let's try and bring down the current one)&quot;<br /> Which, appart from the fact that there is always only just one, maybe two [I'm not even trying to spell that] at a time, mirrors the goal of the Siderealss - just that the reason the BG try to prevent new [I'm not even trying to spell that] (or any powerful precogs, for that matter) is that it locks them in a deterministic universe, not necessarily that they cause the end of the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=627369#post627369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Immaculate Faith had to be set up the way it was, or people would start asking questions about the role the Sidereals played in its creation, and potentially unravel their role in the Usurpation. But still, the Immaculate Faith is also set up that a Sidereal who takes precautions is extremely unlikely to be targeted by Realm hostility. The small chance of an unprepared Sidereal being caught flatfooted by Immaculate faithful is greatly outweighed by the usefulness of having nearly all of Creation as a weapon to turn against the Solars, Lunars, and other enemies of Creation. And while the Immaculate Faith may have been created <i>ex nihilo</i>, the Missionaria Protectiva also represented exploitable tropes being created out of wholecloth and inserted in various worlds' myths for the Bene Gesserit's sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, it's a minor difference - the BG added &quot;levers&quot; into an existing power system, while the Sids created a power system with &quot;levers&quot; in it. Both still use the &quot;levers&quot; to manipulate a power system they have no official influence over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=627369#post627369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kwisatz Haderach</div> </div> </div> </div>Bless You/Gesundheit/Oh, hey, The Thing I Shall Not Spell!<br /> (If anyone was wondering what &quot;[I'm not even trying to spell that]&quot; reffered to - it's this)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=627369#post627369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was being a little tongue-in-cheek about this one, but if I recall correctly, the Bene Gesserit were attempting to produce the Kwisatz Haderach in an attempt to transcend the limitations of humanity that led to people being enslaved by artificial intelligences and by the inherent weaknesses that caused the stagnation of the Old Empire. In this way, the Bene Gesserit were indeed attempting to &quot;save the world&quot; from threats both external and internal.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the &quot;core books&quot;, the reason to create an [I'm not even trying to spell that] isn't really given, except in the &quot;well, human progress!&quot; kind of way: It's a new frontier, someone who can look as far into the past and future as he wants, while they themselves can only look into the past and the navigators only into the future, and neither group can look as far as the [I'm not even trying to spell that].<br /> The war against artificial intelligences is kind of mentioned, but in an &quot;well that's not even worth worrying about any more&quot;-manner. It's pointed out that, by the time of Paul Atreides, humans minds are actually more advanced than the AIs of the past - Baron Harkonnen's mentat mentiones that even the Baron could outthink the &quot;thinking machines&quot; of the past. Note that the mentat literally says &quot;<i>even</i> you&quot; - it's not flattery, the mentat considers himself leages beyond an AI.<br /> On the other hand, that might be propaganda... It's mentioned along with AI being prohibited. And an &quot;We aren't allowed to&quot; alone isn't as efficient as an &quot;We aren't allowed to, and there's no reason to do so anyway&quot;. Or it might be that this was the original reason, and momentum just made them continue trying to create an [I'm not even trying to spell that] even when AI wasn't an issue any more.<br /> <br /> /Edit: I just read a Dune wiki and found out that, apparently, the two mysterious &quot;Enemies&quot; at the end of Chapterhouse of Dune are later (in sequels created by other authors) &quot;revealed&quot; to be the same thinking machines that triggered the Buttlerian Jihad...<br /> Weird, when I read Chapterhouse of Dune, I got the distinct impression that those two beings were Face Dancers. The book had revealed that there were now Face Dancers able to absorb memories, and I think it was implied that those two were Face Dancers who had absorbed thousands of memories, essentially turning them into something worse than Abominations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":7262,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","user":"Amakawa Yuuto","date":". 08-15-2015, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T03:59:27-07:00","id":627462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bene Gesserit shepherd humanity in order to produce a god. The Sidereals shepherd humanity to prevent the return of gods</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, kind of. Maybe also something vaguely similar in that notion of being good at manipulating certain circumstances to create hero figures, but not being very good at predicting or controlling those figures. Seems like a trajectory that the Gold Faction could be on in some instances; creating the circumstances in which a Solar could become an emperor, and then watch in horror as they lose a handle on all of it. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh god, now I'm like 99% certain that Anys Syn is trying to get Ragara Myrun to achieve the Blossom of the Perfected Lotus because it will make him the Kwisatz Haderach.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nah, that can't be it; Anys Syn is already capable of anything that Myrrun would be able to do. He's not getting any special superpowers on account of being a different gender to her. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T06:30:28-07:00","id":627511,"title":"","content":"You can definitely have the Bene Gesserit as an inspiration for Sidereals if you like. I wouldn't say they're not particularly closer than any of the other ultra competant secret societies of sorcerors that haunt fantasy literature and anime, though (for every aspect they're more similar than another, they'll be another where they're less similar).<br /> <br /> Having groups of your descendents to in the long term do things seems overly complicated, fragile, difficult and not particularly interesting to do, so I doubt many Sidereals do it. No reason why you couldn't have a particular NPC do it though - as an idiosyncrasy, preferring to &quot;work&quot; with the emotion bond of a parent to a child isn't really too out there, and in a world like Creation I think many people take ancestor-descendant relationships generally more seriously than present day Western society (to risk a generalisation).<br /> <br /> An idea I toyed with was that the Starblessed could take on Resplendent Destinies with powers as a permanent aspect of their person for motes rather than the points invested into RDs, and were particularly susceptible to astrology (less points for a Sidereal to place a thematic effect on them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T08:41:15-07:00","id":627637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=627011#post627011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if having a child is the simplest or most effective natural way of insinuating into or manipulating a social structure, why would a Sidereal trust that task to someone else? Especially when their own child would prove so much easier a variable to control?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it being their own child needlessly complicates matters. There's a risk of forming a strong emotional attachment to a child whose upbringing will almost certainly need to be entrusted to proxies who might colour their world view in subtle ways.<br /> That's before you even factor how Sidereal Half Caste may or may not work, if you're going by Scroll of Heroes they're creating a mini-exalt and expecting them to be somehow more controllable than a Mortal.<br /> <br /> Oh it's great story fodder, don't get me wrong but this would be the kind of plan rooted in Sidereal Hubris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 08-15-2015, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T09:24:11-07:00","id":627658,"title":"","content":"Hmm, overlooked some stuff... <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that the Sidereals need to remain undercover when working in Creation, one has to imagine that they reserve their supernatural powers for situations that genuinely require them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, no. Even accounting for how stuff like Avoidance Kata or Neighbourhood Relocation Scheme actively obscures its own presence, no Sidereal is giving themselves away by spending their personal motes on Force Decision or something. Or, you know, that whole cascade of Charms that starts with turning invisible and ends with being able to implant suggestions that people assume originated within themselves. Sidereals are tremedously well-equipped for secretly manipulating others into roles and scenarios decided by Destiny. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if having a child is the simplest or most effective natural way of insinuating into or manipulating a social structure, why would a Sidereal trust that task to someone else?</div> </div> </div> </div> They wouldn't? They wouldn't well need to go about personally getting into that role either, because again, manipulation. Jeez, Sidereals can develop the ability to steal other people's social identities; arrange for Catherine d'Medici to be away for a while, swipe her name and put on a dress, and being a man won't be enough to stop her children from thinking that you're their mother. Sidereals are agents of Heaven, accustomed to live amidst splendour and entrusted with the work of God; they don't need to putz around with marriage or child rearing in order to accumulate wealth or social influence. I mean, all of this: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's a fact in human history that children make for exceptional social and political tools. Acting as the regent of a child monarch means that they grow up with a will that is pliant to your wishes -- and even more so when that child is your own, as evinced by queen-mothers such as Catherine de' Medici. Impregnating or being impregnated by a person of higher status has been a method people have used for millennia to climb the social ranks. Having a child with a person creates ties of trust between the parents -- something that can, and likely has, been manipulated before by one party looking for some kind of gain. Creating a child creates a clear line of succession for monarchs and aristocrats. Having many children has historically been seen as a direct corollary of one's wealth, status, and prestige -- the &quot;war of pregnancies&quot; between Leah and Rachel in the Tanach, and between Kaushalya, Sumitra, and Kaikeyi in the Ramayana, were methods by which those aristocratic women jockeyed for status in their society.</div> </div> </div> </div> This feels largely unaware of what the actual powers and duties of the Sidereal Exalted are. Social ranks are a thing that they puppet about from their position amongst the clouds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T12:07:30-07:00","id":627750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=627511#post627511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can definitely have the Bene Gesserit as an inspiration for Sidereals if you like. I wouldn't say they're not particularly closer than any of the other ultra competant secret societies of sorcerors that haunt fantasy literature and anime, though (for every aspect they're more similar than another, they'll be another where they're less similar).<br /> <br /> Having groups of your descendents to in the long term do things seems overly complicated, fragile, difficult and not particularly interesting to do, so I doubt many Sidereals do it. No reason why you couldn't have a particular NPC do it though - as an idiosyncrasy, preferring to &quot;work&quot; with the emotion bond of a parent to a child isn't really too out there, and in a world like Creation I think many people take ancestor-descendant relationships generally more seriously than present day Western society (to risk a generalisation).</div> </div> </div> </div>No doubt with the first part. The Bene Gesserit and Sidereals both draw from the same &quot;evil vizier&quot; trope. And in fact, you could make a very good case about Gendo Ikari and NERV from <i>Neon Genesis Evangelion</i> being similar to the Sidereals thanks to them both participating that same trope. But I think that by this point, it can all be chalked up to subjectivity, and I still see the Bene Gesserit as a useful source of inspiration for Sidereals -- and how Sidereals might behave when their schemes start falling down around one exceptional individual. I also don't think that a Sidereal plot being overly complicated, fragile, and difficult is beyond them. It fits pretty neatly with their hubris and reflects the fact that ever since the Usurpation, the Sidereals have been flying by the seats of their pants. They weren't meant to shadow-rule Creation the way they do, and everything that they've done since has essentially been a jury-rigging of the terms and powers of their original mandate.<br /> <br /> (As a complete aside, I love seeing Gendo Ikari as a very callous Gold Faction Sidereal manipulating some mentally exhausted young Solars into fighting the enemies of Creation.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Originally posted by <b>Lioness</b><br /> I think it being their own child needlessly complicates matters. There's a risk of forming a strong emotional attachment to a child whose upbringing will almost certainly need to be entrusted to proxies who might colour their world view in subtle ways.<br /> That's before you even factor how Sidereal Half Caste may or may not work, if you're going by Scroll of Heroes they're creating a mini-exalt and expecting them to be somehow more controllable than a Mortal.<br /> <br /> Oh it's great story fodder, don't get me wrong but this would be the kind of plan rooted in Sidereal Hubris. </div> </div> </div>I can't imagine any younger, field-agent Sidereals getting a message from their superiors telling them, &quot;For this assignment, we need you to make a baby.&quot; But I could definitely imagine that a callous or pragmatic Sidereal wouldn't feel much risk in bonding with their child, especially when the benefits of having a child for an assignment outweigh the negatives. I think that it would be a choice largely reserved for Saturn- and Venus-castes, though. Children don't really play much of a direct role in transport and communication, or in military tactics; and I think that Jupiter-castes would be more interested in ferreting out the secrets of a person's parentage rather than creating new people. But Chosen of Venus are interested in seduction, families, and reconciliation. Chosen of Saturn are assassins, but are as interested in long-term stability as the other Sidereals, meaning that they also have to be interested in providing stronger branches than the ones they pruned from the tree, as it were.<br /> <br /> I gave an example of a Chosen of Saturn producing a child by a tyrant in order to have someone pliant to put on a throne after they kill the tyrant, but I'll give you an example of what I could see a Chosen of Venus doing. Imagine there are two warring families in a major city of Creation. Family A and Family B have stockpiles of magical weaponry and if their conflict spills out into open warfare, they could devastate the city and the landscape for generations. A Chosen of Serenity is sent in to resolve the mess. He could spend years, maybe decades, attempting to covertly nudge the families into diplomacy. Or he could put on a Resplendent Destiny as the first son of Family A's matriarch, go and seduce the cherished daughter of Family B's patriarch, and then marry and impregnate her. This Chosen of Serenity could then hold up the grandchild of the two warring families as a tie to bind them, and implicitly warn them that if they start war, they run the risk of killing the grandchild produced by their beloved children, since that grandchild is of both houses. There's a chance of that plan failing, but it's very direct, and a well-read Sidereal would know from history that mingling bloodlines is usually the first step in binding aristocratic families into alliances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Originally posted by <b>Isator Levi</b><br /> Yeah, no. Even accounting for how stuff like Avoidance Kata or Neighbourhood Relocation Scheme actively obscures its own presence, no Sidereal is giving themselves away by spending their personal motes on Force Decision or something. Or, you know, that whole cascade of Charms that starts with turning invisible and ends with being able to implant suggestions that people assume originated within themselves. Sidereals are tremedously well-equipped for secretly manipulating others into roles and scenarios decided by Destiny. </div> </div> </div>The Sidereals were chosen by the Maidens because they're hyper-competent even <i>before</i> the Exaltation. A Chosen of Serenity who tends to seduce their targets is likely shockingly good at doing so even without the use of charms. Why would you use the hammer of a charm when you could use the scalpel of a personal talent? I mean, stop to consider that the Sidereals are technically Anathema. If a Sidereal expends at little too much essence and trips the secret magical wards of some Dragon-Blooded sorcerer employed by a tyrant, they might end up with a failed assignment and a Wyld Hunt on their ass. Why risk that when you could seduce the tyrant and poison them to death over several months with arsenic? If I were trained as a marksman by the Marines, that might be an incredibly useful skill, but I wouldn't consider &quot;sniping&quot; as the answer to the question &quot;how am I going to convince the loan officer at the bank to give me a loan?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They wouldn't? They wouldn't well need to go about personally getting into that role either, because again, manipulation. Jeez, Sidereals can develop the ability to steal other people's social identities; arrange for Catherine d'Medici to be away for a while, swipe her name and put on a dress, and being a man won't be enough to stop her children from thinking that you're their mother. Sidereals are agents of Heaven, accustomed to live amidst splendour and entrusted with the work of God; they don't need to putz around with marriage or child rearing in order to accumulate wealth or social influence. I mean, all of this: </div> </div> </div>The very fact that the Sidereals have to continually descend from Heaven to do wetwork in Creation is a sign that they have to do dirty, dreary, and abysmal work as part of their job. But in a society of immortals, I hardly think that a nine-month assignment is something that would really cause most of its members to stamp their feet. It's preferable to accidentally flaring an anima banner where a Realm Dragon-Blooded could see it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This feels largely unaware of what the actual powers and duties of the Sidereal Exalted are. Social ranks are a thing that they puppet about from their position amongst the clouds. </div> </div> </div><i>Sometimes.</i> The Sidereals have to play the part of both \u00e9minance grises and spies, among other roles. And while a vizier and a spy often travel the same paths, there are many times when the two roles are in opposition to one another. Cardinal Richelieu would never have gotten his hands personally dirty when spying on Marie de' Medici, but for the Sidereals, they have to play the both parts -- Richelieu <i>and</i> his spies. Sometimes the situation demands that a Chosen of the Maidens take off their ministerial cap in order to wrap their faces in black and stab someone through the throat with a Starmetal knife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","user":"Kallipolis","date":". 08-15-2015, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T13:40:07-07:00","id":627870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sidereals were chosen by the Maidens because they're hyper-competent even before the Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's got to be one amazing foetus... <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you use the hammer of a charm when you could use the scalpel of a personal talent?</div> </div> </div> </div> False dichotomy. Also, wrong analogy altogether; personally adopting whatever lineage perpetuating role isn't an act of subtlety, it's a significant investment of time and energy. It has to be worth more than &quot;this person I want to control will trust me more if I have their kid in a year&quot;, and the genetics of the Sidereal are unlikely to contribute anything of significance. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why risk that when you could seduce the tyrant and poison them to death over several months with arsenic?</div> </div> </div> </div> At what point does having a baby become necessary to that? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The very fact that the Sidereals have to continually descend from Heaven to do wetwork in Creation is a sign that they have to do dirty, dreary, and abysmal work as part of their job.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is begging the question of what kind of universal quality there is to Sidereal missions that earns this kind of description. It's mostly irrelevant, though; Sidereals are sent into Creation to correct errors in Fate. I can hardly imagine a situation for this where they're not equipped well enough to just go straight for the task rather than &quot;hmm, I've got to weasal my way into an inner circle in order to actually have the resources I need, what's the most efficient method... I know, I'll have somebody's baby&quot;. There's a whole bunch of question marks seperating you from that profit. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">in a society of immortals, I hardly think that a nine-month assignment is something that would really cause most of its members to stamp their feet.</div> </div> </div> </div> You know, I've not even considered the points about how much of an imposition the whole thing is on bodily autonomy. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's preferable to accidentally flaring an anima banner where a Realm Dragon-Blooded could see it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Spending Essence does not work that way. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sidereals have to play the part of both \u00e9minance grises and spies, among other roles. And while a vizier and a spy often travel the same paths, there are many times when the two roles are in opposition to one another. Cardinal Richelieu would never have gotten his hands personally dirty when spying on Marie de' Medici, but for the Sidereals, they have to play the both parts -- Richelieu and his spies. Sometimes the situation demands that a Chosen of the Maidens take off their ministerial cap in order to wrap their faces in black and stab someone through the throat with a Starmetal knife.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think you're still not quite getting what I'm saying. If a Sidereal needs to work their way into somebody's social circle in order to accomplish something, there are numerous far more effective methods of doing that than personally going through the mundanities, not least of which is being able to steal the role out from somebody who already has it. There <i>may</i> be occasions in which an individual Sidereal opts for an approach like becoming the parent to somebody's heir, but it's not going to be anywhere close to a standard operating procedure like it is with the Bene Gesserit, because there are so many reasons <i>not to do it</i>. That is only if the child itself is the end; using a child as a means to an end of some other form of social closeness? Having somebody's child so that they'll trust you enough to poison them? That is ludicrously circuitous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T14:33:12-07:00","id":627925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=627750#post627750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No doubt with the first part. The Bene Gesserit and Sidereals both draw from the same &quot;evil vizier&quot; trope. And in fact, you could make a very good case about Gendo Ikari and NERV from <i>Neon Genesis Evangelion</i> being similar to the Sidereals thanks to them both participating that same trope. But I think that by this point, it can all be chalked up to subjectivity, and I still see the Bene Gesserit as a useful source of inspiration for Sidereals -- and how Sidereals might behave when their schemes start falling down around one exceptional individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, or they can be <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Declare\" target=\"_blank\">Operation Declare </a>or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Work_of_Time\" target=\"_blank\">The Otherhood</a> or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood_Blockade_Battlefront\" target=\"_blank\">Libra</a> or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hellsing\" target=\"_blank\">The Royal Order of Protestant Knights</a> or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watcher_(Buffy_the_Vampire_Slayer)\" target=\"_blank\">the Watchers</a>, or whatever <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AncientOrderOfProtectors\" target=\"_blank\">Ancient Order of Protectors </a>you fancy.<br /> <br /> The Bene Gesserit are a parallel, but I do think that they seem much more engaged with shaping the ruling aristocracy of Dune than the Sidereals are to the Dragonblooded Dynasty (for example), where the Sidereals have to my mind more of a high end deal at the top with the Empress to shape the broad mandate of the Realm and Immaculate Philosophy, then they hotfix where needed, rather than a state where they are carefully managing the Dynasty at an intricate level (don't nobody got time for dat). Although more or less like you say YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T15:12:00-07:00","id":628017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=627870#post627870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's got to be one amazing foetus...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're actually kind of right, facetiousness aside. The Maidens are goddesses of <i>time and destiny</i>. They're only tangentially bound by linear time. Their Sidereals are chosen because the Maidens have a good idea of what they can do before they're even born. It creates a chicken-and-egg situation because one has to ask if it's their exceptional nature that grants them the Exaltation, or whether their future Exaltation affects their early nature, but the temporal questions can be sidestepped by asserting, simply, that the Sidereals really are hyper-competent before their Exaltation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> False dichotomy. Also, wrong analogy altogether; personally adopting whatever lineage perpetuating role isn't an act of subtlety, it's a significant investment of time and energy. It has to be worth more than &quot;this person I want to control will trust me more if I have their kid in a year&quot;, and the genetics of the Sidereal are unlikely to contribute anything of significance. </div> </div> </div>Says you. Neither you nor I, though, have ever been secret agents, so artificially limiting what spies are willing to do to get the job done seems preemptive. I will say that there have been plenty of revealed spies in history who have married and had children, only to use their families as deep cover for their real activities, so it's not <i>bizarre</i> for a Sidereal to do the same, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At what point does having a baby become necessary to that? </div> </div> </div>I was using it as an analogy. I can use another one to make my point more clearly: In Vampire: the Masquerade, a Ventrue Prince could easily command loyalty from the city's vampire population using Dominate regularly. But it's considered a mark of weakness and laziness in that Prince, and it's very likely that relying on the crutch of supernatural powers will blunt that Prince's personal skills when someone immune to their Dominate abilities shows up in their city.<br /> <br /> I imagine that if a Sidereal has the luxury of choosing between mundane methods and supernatural ones to solve their problems, they're likely to go for the mundane solution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is begging the question of what kind of universal quality there is to Sidereal missions that earns this kind of description. It's mostly irrelevant, though; Sidereals are sent into Creation to correct errors in Fate. I can hardly imagine a situation for this where they're not equipped well enough to just go straight for the task rather than &quot;hmm, I've got to weasal my way into an inner circle in order to actually have the resources I need, what's the most efficient method... I know, I'll have somebody's baby&quot;. There's a whole bunch of question marks seperating you from that profit. </div> </div> </div>Ahn-Aru in the 2e sourcebook had an assignment with an indefinite duration. I don't find it odd to consider that a being with a 5,000 year lifespan might be given assignments that last years and decades. The conception of a child might just be one thread in the elaborate decades-long tapestry a Sidereal weaves against a kingdom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know, I've not even considered the points about how much of an imposition the whole thing is on bodily autonomy. </div> </div> </div>Like I said to Lioness, I can't imagine that Yu-Shan would ever order one of the Sidereals to create a child. But I can imagine a Sidereal freely choosing to do so for the sake of a plot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spending Essence does not work that way. </div> </div> </div>Hell, I wouldn't want to risk spending motes from my Peripheral Essence pool with the Dragon-Blooded around. Would you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you're still not quite getting what I'm saying. If a Sidereal needs to work their way into somebody's social circle in order to accomplish something, there are numerous far more effective methods of doing that than personally going through the mundanities, not least of which is being able to steal the role out from somebody who already has it. There <i>may</i> be occasions in which an individual Sidereal opts for an approach like becoming the parent to somebody's heir, but it's not going to be anywhere close to a standard operating procedure like it is with the Bene Gesserit, because there are so many reasons <i>not to do it</i>. That is only if the child itself is the end; using a child as a means to an end of some other form of social closeness? Having somebody's child so that they'll trust you enough to poison them? That is ludicrously circuitous. </div> </div> </div>I gave an example to Lioness where the creation of a child would be an easier and more direct solution than other methods. Now, I will admit that I find it unlikely that any of the Sidereals other than the Chosen of Venus or Saturn would use it as a method, but I think you're unnecessarily limiting what the Sidereals would do to achieve a goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T15:25:56-07:00","id":628034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=628017#post628017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Says you. Neither you nor I, though, have ever been secret agents, so artificially limiting what spies are willing to do to get the job done seems preemptive. I will say that there have been plenty of revealed spies in history who have married and had children, only to use their families as deep cover for their real activities, so it's not <i>bizarre</i> for a Sidereal to do the same, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>No historical spy had access to Sidereal charms, Sorcery, supernatural Martial Arts, or Sidereal astrology. They were much more limited in their means. That doesn't mean Sidereals would never have a kid as part of a scheme, but that they will not often need to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T15:30:53-07:00","id":628039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=628034#post628034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No historical spy had access to Sidereal charms, Sorcery, supernatural Martial Arts, or Sidereal astrology. They were much more limited in their means. That doesn't mean Sidereals would never have a kid as part of a scheme, but that they will not often need to.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, of course not. I imagine that a Sidereal who relied on creating illegitimate children to further their plots would quickly be regarded as either an asshole or unsettlingly eccentric in Yu-Shan and attract the censure of their superiors -- a sudden spate of dispossessed Star-Blessed running around Creation would be something of a headache for the Bureau of Destiny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T16:48:03-07:00","id":628116,"title":"","content":"Sidereals are not spies; they're sorcerer-bureaucrat enforcers of Destiny. They get involved in people's lives almost solely to correct them on to the course of Destiny. There are only a hundred of them. These things need to be considered to maintain coherence in portraying them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T17:15:48-07:00","id":628143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=628116#post628116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals are not spies; they're sorcerer-bureaucrat enforcers of Destiny. They get involved in people's lives almost solely to correct them on to the course of Destiny. There are only a hundred of them. These things need to be considered to maintain coherence in portraying them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerer-bureaucrat-enforcers-of-Destiny-spy-ninja-assassin-kung-fu-master-viziers. All of the Chosen of the Maidens -- with the exception of the Chosen of Mars -- are spies in some way: Mercury's Chosen transmit and intercept information, and of create disinformation between parties. The Chosen of Venus are heaven's honeypots, seducing targets into giving up secret information and becoming amenable to what the Sidereals need them to do. Jupiter's Chosen infiltrate stores of private and confidential information in order to use them to the Sidereals' advantage. The Chosen of Saturn are, among other things, straight-up assassins, covertly killing individuals in order to change the political landscape of a place.<br /> <br /> With the exception of Mars' Chosen, they all spy when Destiny demands they do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T18:06:09-07:00","id":628155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=628143#post628143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the exception of Mars' Chosen, they all spy when Destiny demands they do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not forget military intelligence (no matter how much fun is made of that term). Mars' Chosen don't just blindly bash in heads, they're also strategists, and with Archery and Athletics as Caste Abilities, they're just one Favourited Ability away from being awesome sniper-assassins - or instigators of revolts and spreader of propaganda using Presence, another Caste Ability.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, these are all just one part of their jobs - while individual sids might specialise in them, others might ignore them. They might not get to choose their jobs, but I'd bet they do get to choose how to approach them.<br /> <br /> (Also, the precision of &quot;Destiny's demands&quot; - and, indeed, the precision of the Maiden's ability to predict the future - varies from table to table. And I remember a dev saying that Samsara isn't going to be a thing in 3ed, so no overarching &quot;Better than fate&quot; super-destiny, either)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T18:24:32-07:00","id":628163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=628155#post628155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not forget military intelligence (no matter how much fun is made of that term). Mars' Chosen don't just blindly bash in heads, they're also strategists, and with Archery and Athletics as Caste Abilities, they're just one Favourited Ability away from being awesome sniper-assassins - or instigators of revolts and spreader of propaganda using Presence, another Caste Ability.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, these are all just one part of their jobs - while individual sids might specialise in them, others might ignore them. They might not get to choose their jobs, but I'd bet they do get to choose how to approach them.<br /> <br /> (Also, the precision of &quot;Destiny's demands&quot; - and, indeed, the precision of the Maiden's ability to predict the future - varies from table to table. And I remember a dev saying that Samsara isn't going to be a thing in 3ed, so no overarching &quot;Better than fate&quot; super-destiny, either)</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't add the Chosen of Mars to the &quot;spy&quot; category because I always saw them as being figures whose talents make them best at coordinating and utilizing the spying skills of the other Sidereals. For example, a Mars-Chosen general could use a Chosen of Mercury to control supply lines and the information that comes in and out of the battlefield. That general could use a Chosen of Venus to break the morale of the enemy's soldiers before a battle. A Chosen of Jupiter could relay information about the numbers, tactics, and armaments of the enemy to the Chosen of Mars. And if all else failed, the Mars-Chosen general could use a Chosen of Saturn to surgically assassinate enemy officers in order to tilt the balance of power in favor of their side.<br /> <br /> Could the Chosen of Mars be spies and solitary assassins? Sure. But I think that they're the most &quot;team player&quot; of the Sidereal castes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T19:28:11-07:00","id":628174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=628163#post628163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could the Chosen of Mars be spies and solitary assassins? Sure. But I think that they're the most &quot;team player&quot; of the Sidereal castes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not forget:<br /> Sidereals are, first and foremost, people. There's a Joybringer whose greatest joy is bashing Fair Folk with an iron morningstar.<br /> <br /> Shoehorning <i>any</i> caste into a single role does it gross injustice. And the combination of utility arrows, athletics, and having stealth favoured would allow a choosen of battle to rain pure havoc (or love, or rain, or a fondness of puppies) on whoever is in the way of their goal, without even being seen. Their caste abilities lend themselves <i>better</i> to playing assassins then the Endings caste's when it comes to killing someone from a distance. And up cloce, because melee is their thing, too. All they need is stealth.<br /> <br /> <br /> Endings, on the other hand, have bureaucracy as a caste ability, making those that care for it as good as Journeys in intercepting messeges, as long as they get a foot into the door of whatever organisation they're shadowing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":7262,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","user":"Amakawa Yuuto","date":". 08-15-2015, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T19:47:55-07:00","id":628178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=628174#post628174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not forget:<br /> Sidereals are, first and foremost, people. There's a Joybringer whose greatest joy is bashing Fair Folk with an iron morningstar.<br /> <br /> Shoehorning <i>any</i> caste into a single role does it gross injustice. And the combination of utility arrows, athletics, and having stealth favoured would allow a choosen of battle to rain pure havoc (or love, or rain, or a fondness of puppies) on whoever is in the way of their goal, without even being seen. Their caste abilities lend themselves <i>better</i> to playing assassins then the Endings caste's when it comes to killing someone from a distance. And up cloce, because melee is their thing, too. All they need is stealth.<br /> <br /> <br /> Endings, on the other hand, have bureaucracy as a caste ability, making those that care for it as good as Journeys in intercepting messeges, as long as they get a foot into the door of whatever organisation they're shadowing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you insofar as the Exalted would have been useless to the gods if they were merely automata without any freedom to choose. But I think because the Sidereals are shepherded from before they were born by goddesses of destiny into the role of Exalted, they fit their &quot;caste archetypes&quot; more closely than other Exalted. If I had to draw a chart, it'd look like this:<br /> <br /> (Adheres closest to caste archetype)<br /> Sidereals<br /> -<br /> Terrestrials<br /> -<br /> Lunars<br /> -<br /> Solars, Abyssals, Infernals<br /> -<br /> Alchemicals<br /> (Adheres least to caste archetype)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T20:05:29-07:00","id":628182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=628178#post628178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think because the Sidereals are shepherded from before they were born by goddesses of destiny into the role of Exalted,</div> </div> </div> </div>The degree of this &quot;shepherding&quot; isn't really specified, and it's definitely not stated to to cause a stronger &quot;caste-adherence&quot; than in other Exalts. The only difference is that the books say &quot;Other Exalts get chosen because they fit their caste, Sidereals are destined for a caste and develop fitting personalities&quot; - but with explicit exceptions.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=628178#post628178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they fit their &quot;caste archetypes&quot; more closely than other Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, Iron Siaka.<br /> Huge, muscle-bound, her definition of &quot;fun&quot; is bashing her enemies, especially all Creatures of Darkness (not just Fair Folk, my mistake) with weapons in melee. She's a Joybringer, and yet her strongest abilities in her writeup are &quot;Martial Arts&quot; and &quot;Melee&quot;, both 5. (Dodge is 4, and Performance is 3 (Prayer +2), those two being her best &quot;in-caste&quot; abilities)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":7262,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","user":"Amakawa Yuuto","date":". 08-15-2015, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T20:52:33-07:00","id":628191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=628182#post628182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, Iron Siaka.<br /> Huge, muscle-bound, her definition of &quot;fun&quot; is bashing her enemies, especially all Creatures of Darkness (not just Fair Folk, my mistake) with weapons in melee. She's a Joybringer, and yet her strongest abilities in her writeup are &quot;Martial Arts&quot; and &quot;Melee&quot;, both 5. (Dodge is 4, and Performance is 3 (Prayer +2), those two being her best &quot;in-caste&quot; abilities)</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Welllllll.</i> Even goddesses of fate and destiny aren't always 100% on the mark. Maybe Mars was too busy winning the Games of Divinity to personally pick Siaka for Team Red?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T22:08:09-07:00","id":628207,"title":"","content":"Is this the perennial issue on the forum where we use caste names to describe character archetypes that don't necessarily match the actual caste of the Exalt?<br /> <br /> For example, the way people use Dawn to refer to the Solars that have a bunch of combat charms and can solo mortal armies even though for most of them were Nights and Twilights in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T02:16:55-07:00","id":628408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the way people use Dawn to refer to the Solars that have a bunch of combat charms and can solo mortal armies even though for most of them were Nights and Twilights in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div> That was more a case of mechanics not really reflecting a desired reality of the setting. Saying &quot;Joybringers are always incredible seducers!&quot; is more along the lines of looking at Lunars having Intelligence Charms and assuming that it makes them the ultimate philosophers; it's not just a matter of reductive Castes, but misunderstanding what archetypes and aptitudes are actually associated with the Exalted in question. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a Joybringer whose greatest joy is bashing Fair Folk with an iron morningstar.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure and plenty of Fair Folk and other monsters are the source of suffering to countless people. There are more ways to bring people joy than to have sex with them. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mercury's Chosen transmit and intercept information, and of create disinformation between parties. The Chosen of Venus are heaven's honeypots, seducing targets into giving up secret information and becoming amenable to what the Sidereals need them to do. Jupiter's Chosen infiltrate stores of private and confidential information in order to use them to the Sidereals' advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, you... don't really get Sidereals. None of this is really part of their function, or even all that necessary. A whole bunch of those things you're talking about can be covered by rudimentary examination of the Loom or a single Investigation Charm, and the rest can probably be gotten from the gods who work alongside them. Sidereal Castes are not about using the essential quality of your Caste to do everything, they're about overseeing that thing's presence in the world. Honestly, the Chosen of Serenity really tend to get the shaft when people imagine what they're about as opposed to actually examining sample characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T03:48:09-07:00","id":628422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=628408#post628408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure and plenty of Fair Folk and other monsters are the source of suffering to countless people. There are more ways to bring people joy than to have sex with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>See this is the kind of stupidity you end up saying when you're an otherwise intelligent person who embraces memes like &quot;Sidereals manage their domains, they don't *do* them&quot; as a hard dogma. Iron Siaka is beating demons in the face as an extension of &quot;managing&quot; joy? Wtf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T03:50:57-07:00","id":628423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=628191#post628191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Welllllll.</i> Even goddesses of fate and destiny aren't always 100% on the mark. Maybe Mars was too busy winning the Games of Divinity to personally pick Siaka for Team Red?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals are not chosen. They are destined. Specifically, their exaltations were put onto people with great and appropriate destinies. Iron Siaka is perhaps destined to bring great happiness* to the world, not to bring great battles to the world (bearing in mind of course, that the job of Sidereals is to oversee destiny, so she may not actually do so: destiny doesn't always happen as planned. It's just that she's supposed to). Possibly she'll do so by winning a war and thus bringing peace. Perhaps she'll get kids into martial arts, and they'll enjoy it a lot. Possibly she just really enjoys hitting people, and coincidentally this has nothing to do with her destiny.<br /> <br /> *I recognise this is a simplified version of how the Joybringers work.<br /> <br /> As Isator said, the primary job of Sidereals is to oversee things, not be good at them or necessarily do them themselves. A lot of the time they will be good at them because it helps, but not always. A Chosen of Journeys has a knack for travelling, but her actual job isn't travelling, it's to make sure that people in Creation travel as Fate decrees.* So she might encourage the Guild to do more caravans, or encourage a road-building company, or encourage the Realm to invest more money in shipping. It probably helps if she has, say, Sail, so she understands how ships work, but it doesn't necessarily mean she actually will need to do a lot of Sailing. However, she can use her Sail charms to make deals with Water spirits to ensure the smooth operation of a shipping concern (this why Sidereal charms are not necessarily very direct applications of that ability).<br /> A Chosen of Battles has a knack for fighting and war, but his job is primarily to make sure wars happen at the right time, between the right people, and the right people win. He might do this by spreading rumours or propaganda. He might do it by sabotaging supply lines or assassinating generals that are too good/bad. He might get some war gods to send dreams to their worshippers encouraging war. He might pay mercenaries to attack a neighbouring country dressed in fake uniforms. Only very occasionally is he likely to actually lead a company in a war between mortals in Creation. He's much more likely to pretend to be a regular soldier, and use his War charms to buff the side that Destiny has decreed should win.<br /> <br /> *This is rather complicated by the fact that the gameline has never quite agreed on what Fate and Destiny actually involve, but there you go.<br /> <br /> The secondary job of Sidereals, of course, is thwarting the enemies of Fate; demons, fae and ghosts. So Iron Siaka's pretty damn good at that, which makes Venus's department look better (most Joybringers have no particular knack for combat, so when it comes to rounding up a posse to put down a second circle demon that escaped from Hell because some idiot had sex with a virgin in her weaving room, or whatever, Iron Siaka can represent her bureau, so the departments of War or Endings don't complain that the Joybringers don't pull their weight and demand its funding is reallocated to them. So Iron Siaka probably makes the other Joybringers happy that way).<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, lastly, I want to address Kallilopolis's point about caste stereotypes. I'd say the ones that adhere least to their archetype is Dragonblood, because they don't have Castes, they have Aspects. Their aspects are just determined by their blood (I'd say it's genetic, but that'll annoy people: still, you know what I mean). There's some effects on their personality, but not massively (there's more cultural pressure).<br /> Think of the signature characters on the front. Pelleps Delled is an unbending fanatic, not what you expect from a Water aspect. There are two master generals as signature characters: an Air aspect, and a Wood aspect. The arrogant sorcerer who does whatever it takes to get power is an Earth aspect.<br /> Essentially, you can take any personality or character type and put it in any Aspect. Whereas a master doctor who's dedicated his life to researching medicine is not going to exalt as a Dawn, nor is a tribal chief who loves war and fighting but is as dumb as a pile of bricks going to exalt as a Twilight. After exalting, they're likely to train in those things they suddenly find easier (a bookish nerd who exalts as a Wood Aspect might start horse riding and playing music, because he finds them easier than he did before... or he might not, because he still doesn't like them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-16-2015, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T07:49:31-07:00","id":628631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=628408#post628408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you... don't really get Sidereals. None of this is really part of their function, or even all that necessary. A whole bunch of those things you're talking about can be covered by rudimentary examination of the Loom or a single Investigation Charm, and the rest can probably be gotten from the gods who work alongside them. Sidereal Castes are not about using the essential quality of your Caste to do everything, they're about overseeing that thing's presence in the world. Honestly, the Chosen of Serenity really tend to get the shaft when people imagine what they're about as opposed to actually examining sample characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all disagreeing with you, I just want to <i>really</i> point out that you're quoting the wrong person there. You're responding to Kallipolis' post <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=628163#post628163\">here</a>, not me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T08:09:34-07:00","id":628664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">See this is the kind of stupidity you end up saying when you're an otherwise intelligent person who embraces memes like &quot;Sidereals manage their domains, they don't *do* them&quot; as a hard dogma.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well... thank you................. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iron Siaka is beating demons in the face as an extension of &quot;managing&quot; joy? Wtf?</div> </div> </div> </div> The fuck is that Chosen of Serenity have responsibility for the health, happiness and general wellbeing of the world. Monsters from outside of Creation are a threat to those things, so why wouldn't there be a Joybringer who takes up the role of destroying them? Quite the comprehensible fuck, if you ask me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T08:31:04-07:00","id":628680,"title":"","content":"Iron Siaka as a joybringer always made loads of sense to me. She enjoys beating the shit out of things and impressing young women with how awesomely cool she is, after all. She protects the happiness of others by beating the shit out of things.<br /> <br /> One of my unused Sidereal concepts is a Joybringer who voluntarily joined a fight-club style gladiatorial arena. The roar of the crowd! The rush of the fight! The adoration of the masses, the money, the contracts, the success, the power! A character like that would be an unusual Chosen of Serenity, but only in the sense that it's an unusual thing for someone to become addicted to fighting in gladiatorial bloodsports.<br /> <br /> Actually I tend to find that making Sidereal characters is pretty easy. The Castes are not very restrictive, if you apply some imagination to them. After all, they are Sidereals. Lateral, conceptual looks at the various Departments and what they represent mean that you can have a midwife as a Chosen of Endings and it be entire consistent. Always liked that about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T08:36:28-07:00","id":628683,"title":"","content":"I was brainstorming the idea of a social-first Chosen of Battles who focuses mostly on social and philosophical conflicts and enjoys debating as much for its own sake as for persuading somebody else of her viewpoint. She probably wouldn't study much War or learn to be a great military strategist. She wouldn't be useless or weak in a physical fight, and she'd still be capable of undertaking fight-manipulating missions for the Crimson Banner, but it wouldn't be her main focus. Come to think of it, she'd probably get pretty good at war propaganda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-16-2015, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T08:42:34-07:00","id":628692,"title":"","content":"I feel like having played MtAw makes applying Sidereal concepts to a wide breadth of characters a lot easier.<br /> <br /> Like, for me, if I am thinking about Battles characters, then the Adamantine Arrow has loads of examples of ways to apply a variety of concepts to the Caste, including many without much martial capability at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T12:45:23-07:00","id":628970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=628664#post628664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The fuck is that Chosen of Serenity have responsibility for the health, happiness and general wellbeing of the world. Monsters from outside of Creation are a threat to those things, so why wouldn't there be a Joybringer who takes up the role of destroying them? Quite the comprehensible fuck, if you ask me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really have a problem with the idea that Iron Siaka is fighting demons for the wellbeing of people. But.. like, is the Chosen of Battles who does so *not* doing so for the wellbeing of people? Is Iron Siaka really fighting demons because they might cause people to experience suffering or happiness at times which are improper for destiny, and cause chaos within the Caste domain which she manages?<br /> <br /> Sidereals have a general responsibility for Fate, and act as people, much more than they manage very specific Caste domains.Their Caste domains are expressed much more through their specific skills, proclivities and abilities rather than as a mission particular to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T03:52:28-07:00","id":629787,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, some of the topics brought up in this thread complement a few other things I've been observing lately that have caused me to have an increasing sense that typical seduction narratives (or even &quot;distract somebody with pretty face&quot; ones) are kind of... stupid.<br /> <br /> It starts off with something as low as a Friends episodes in which a couple of guys can't manage to leave a gym or a bank because a pretty woman is rolled out for them, and goes up to more run of the mill spy fiction in which groups of characters form elaborate plans that hinge on how their one female member will absolutely stand out in an environment in which pretty people tend to be standard, with a mark who can then be distracted or drawn away or whatever.<br /> <br /> The types of that latter one are especially stupid when they take the form of &quot;yeah, just walk into the club/ballroom/pool party and wait to fortuitously catch the eye of the target&quot;. It's... pretty lazy.<br /> <br /> It also crossed with me having seen A View to a Kill a couple of days ago, with the one part in which May Day goes to have sex with Bond. Not even seduce him, really, just go to his bedroom, undress and get under the covers with him. I mean... why? What does that actually accomplish for anybody? I know somebody will say something to the effect of &quot;oh, it's to get him off his guard or establish a kind of power dynamic or something&quot;, and y'know, in real life that kind of thing tends to be just done with prostitutes. It's weird for a person in anything like that position to do it themselves. Perhaps May Day just wanted to get a piece of that sexy Roger Moore action...<br /> <br /> But that's just one part, it's mostly just the whole &quot;draw or distract somebody with sexual flaunting&quot; thing, which the more I think about it the more distractingly improbable it seems to me. The whole thing seems so haphazard and impersonal that it makes me wonder exactly what kind of person could ever fall for it. It's not just about when it's at some kind of party in which there's a whole bunch of attractive people who the one character stands out amongst for some reason, it's also when targets are often wealth and influential people who really don't need to exert much effort to have attractive company without being fleeced, or the possibility of coming on too strongly in a manner that puts people on their guard.<br /> <br /> I feel as one of the more egregious examples was in that dumb GI Joe sequel.<br /> <br /> &quot;All right Adrianne Palicki, you're the woman in the team, so you're up for getting this one guy we need. Just slap on some shorts and a sports bra and walk up to him, and let nature take its course.&quot;<br /> &quot;That sounds good and all, but what do we do if he's ever seen a woman jogging ever?&quot;<br /> &quot;Then may God help us all.&quot;<br /> <br /> See, doesn't it sound incredibly stupid when it's just mildly framed in terms of what a person's actual context would be?<br /> <br /> Or the annoying Friends thing... has anybody ever known somebody to actually act like that? To be rendered incoherent and easily plied just by a generically attractive person (as opposed to somebody specific whom they've formed an attraction to, probably after some extended contact) standing in front of them? I can't really picture it.<br /> <br /> I'll be interested to see what the social influence system makes of things like this; it would probably have to make a few allowances for genre conventions, but as it stands the implications of needing setup and to interact with existing Intimacies (or work to build new ones) seems to have promise in making something a bit more grounded and real. I'm mostly okay with the idea of Solars having something to abstract in the idea of having some indefinable eye-catching quality, to command the attention of a room (and especially its most prominent members) just be walking in.<br /> <br /> Doesn't really seem to be part of the Sidereal milieu, so they have to take the long route (if it's even a situation where that could work).<br /> <br /> Just as a final note to this rambling piece, I recalled that thread from a while back about seduction, and of how towards the end somebody asked how it would work in a manner that wouldn't come across as skeevy.<br /> <br /> At this stage, I think the answer to that question is &quot;when the people involved are already openly interested in having sex with one another&quot;. Seduction in terms of playing up a scenario in which you use cues and visuals to entice a partner, of relaxing and stimulating them, I'd say that's all right.<br /> <br /> Seduction in terms of kind of luring and manipulating a person with whom you are otherwise uninvolved into sex with you is the one I think is creepy and weird.<br /> <br /> This having nothing to do with casual sex, which as far as I understand tends to be... casual. Something the people involved don't make a big song and dance over at any stage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T07:57:01-07:00","id":629940,"title":"","content":"Yeah, when you lay it out like that... the concept is rather stupid, and if writers mostly use women for it it's sexist too. The woman's &quot;job&quot; is to get laid ... because she has nothing better to contribute to a mission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-17-2015, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T09:06:04-07:00","id":629978,"title":"","content":"I also have to wonder at that point about spies seducing people for information, given how the most well known real life example of such a method, Margaretha MacLeod, aka Mata Hari, was kind of infamously ineffective, acquiring little information of worth and being exposed in fairly short order.<br /> <br /> I suppose that, given some of the wording used prior, one might have been thinking of occasions in which an operative goes for a deep cover, with an unassuming family identity that can be used to hide in plain sight, which is pretty different from being seductive and usually implies an investment of <i>decades</i> (also is usually confined to the periphery of what is being watched; it tends to actually be kind of difficult to spy on somebody you live very closely with).<br /> <br /> That there is another rub to the idea of a Sidereal having a child for the sake of getting in on the life of a ruler or whatever; the bizarre assumption that the actual pregnancy is the only matter of concern, rather than everything that needs to happen afterwards.<br /> <br /> &quot;Aha, I've managed to convince this monarch to take me on as consort, and have even sealed the deal by shooting out a kid. Glad that year's over with, time to get back to Heaven and report in.&quot;<br /> &quot;What, you're just going to disappear? Right after having a monarch's child?&quot;<br /> &quot;Yeah, so?&quot;<br /> &quot;And you think that you can pop back in five or six months and pick up where you left off without anybody having any questions? Do you not know how little privacy consorts tend to have, both for security purposes and the traditional mistrust of rulers? Do you know how difficult it is to have an afternoon to yourself without somebody marking your absence? I mean, I know you're a Sidereal, these guards and walls aren't much of an obstacle to you, but when you're gone what's the explanation going to be? 'Oh, Mommy just wanted to pop out for a postnatal spa treatment for most of a year, but we'll be keeping her chair and tiara waiting nicely for when she gets back'?&quot;<br /> &quot;Hmm, I may not have thought this plan to ingratiate myself with the local powers through, considering everything else I've got to do. I mean, I started a revolutionary group in Great Forks that I should probably check in on.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not really an effective application of resources. Not unless there would be some specific quality of the Sidereal's child that they want to insert into any given situation (to once more reiterate what part of the point of the Bene Gesserit was, it wasn't just about ingratiating themselves with the Landstaad and the House of Corrin, it was about being able to control their lines of descent; Lady Jessica was assigned to Duke Atriedes because she was a child of Baron Harknonnen, and the group wanted a merging of those bloodlines which couldn't happen any other way on account of them being sworn enemies. This is a conceit that is largely absent from Exalted, and to the extent that Sidereals would ever need to arrange for any family lines to cross over they would have much better luck with just manipulating other people into doing it).<br /> <br /> This all goes back to what I was saying from the beginning, about how even if it's useful to examine the influences of Exalted, it still needs to be assessed according to its own context, rather than being a generic slate to just project whatever on wants onto. That was the problem of the Lunars throughout Second Edition. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, when you lay it out like that... the concept is rather stupid, and if writers mostly use women for it it's sexist too. The woman's &quot;job&quot; is to get laid ... because she has nothing better to contribute to a mission.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes me think of Gangs of New York, in which Amsterdam Vellon's plan to work his way into the inner circle of the man he wants to kill is based on gradually building himself up, of doing some audacious jobs and putting himself out there when they're offering tribute and an extended series of alternating between deference and speaking out with advice, as well as seizing on unexpected opportunities (namely saving his target from another assassin). Like, he's setting himself up as a criminal protege rather than a false romantic interest, but it's still something more developed and interesting than &quot;walk through the club and wait for serendipity to draw the target to you&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or hell, for an actual example of romantic manipulation, there's Dirty Rotten Scoundrels, in which Michael Caine's experienced con man has contacts throughout the businesses and police of the French Riviera in order to be specifically aware of places in which wealthy women with boring marriages will be attending casinos, with a routine in which he has a bunch of people &quot;let slip&quot; that he's a prince and a freedom fighter and all kinds of romantic escapist fantasy stuff. I'd say there's even a point about trying to look innocuous and be ignored prior to the sudden reveal, so that his marks feel more clever for figuring it out.<br /> <br /> I guess on that note I'll acknowledge the likelihood of confidence tricks that are at least partially built on feigning interest, but any good confidence trickster knows that it requires a lot of set up to lure people into thinking that the scenario is plausible and making them comfortable with giving something up, that it's generally something that you have to keep an eye out for particularly susceptible folks and adjust for opportunities rather than focusing on particular targets, and that you can't keep the con running too long and need to get out of there quickly before the mark starts really examining it or somebody smarter who is close to them catches wind.<br /> <br /> It's more complicated than &quot;be attractive, lure to somewhere unseen&quot; or &quot;have sex, get information/keys&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T19:15:38-07:00","id":630564,"title":"","content":"Do Sidereals have a good way to disguise themselves as a specific real person? If they did they could insert themselves into a prior relationship (discovered via Socialize charms) to exploit interest or trust that already exists, while allowing the other people to do the work building that trust and interest. That is if they needed to seduce somebody specifically to get information out of them and for some reason didn't have a better opportunity to get info.<br /> <br /> If they want to breed two people for some reason, the &quot;simplest&quot; brute-force method is to use Socialize (or Archery!) charms to make them get together -- assuming they don't care about the social and political context these people live in. Manipulating people in more subtle ways, and trying getting their relatives on-board with the relationship, also seems possible with Sidereal abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T19:21:38-07:00","id":630567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=630564#post630564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Sidereals have a good way to disguise themselves as a specific real person?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever since they broke the Mask, <i>any</i> Disguise roll is only Difficulty 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T03:41:19-07:00","id":630918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=630567#post630567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ever since they broke the Mask, <i>any</i> Disguise roll is only Difficulty 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't recall the Second Edition rules, but the First Edition one specifically says that the bonuses don't apply to pretending to be somebody who already exists.<br /> <br /> The 2.5 errata gave Name-Pilfering Practice the ability to let a Sidereal more easily disguise themselves as somebody whose name they've stolen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T03:56:35-07:00","id":630930,"title":"","content":"I'm looking at Cash and Murder Games, and considering how it's not only a meaningful substitute to certain ideas of seduction, but can also skip over much sense of needing some conditional thing like a child to bind a relationship; you can just write them a fate of being bound to you in such a manner (sure it's possible to resist, but there will be plenty of circumstances in which that isn't really called for).<br /> <br /> You and Yours Stance is also the appropriately Sidereal rendition of that idea of a Charm to make one eye-catching in a room (including the points of how it works indiscriminately, obscures the identity of the Sidereal, and makes those who see them a bit extreme).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">assuming they don't care about the social and political context these people live in.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Well that's what Life Without Compunction is for!</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T05:08:30-07:00","id":631049,"title":"","content":"After reading over all this, it strikes me that Heaven wouldn't really want Sidereals to have connections like children. Sids are expected to be able to allow (or force) the massacre of entire cities, to preside over the death-pangs of empires. if you go with the 2E interpretation, that included literally planning human history on a large scale (hope that gets changed).<br /> <br /> People who make those kinds of decisions don't really benefit from having kids. It's one thing when you are a leader in your own nation. Then making your nation powerful helps protect your kids. In the case of Sids, they may be called upon to bring about the genocide of their personal dynasty. In the real world, we call that a potential conflict of interest.<br /> <br /> This sounds like really good story fodder to me. You can play it one of a few ways.<br /> 1. Heaven has directives specifically forbidding anyone working with the Bureau of Destiny from reproducing. In the event they do, the child is killed/taken away. Lots of interesting &quot;going rogue to save my kid&quot; stories there, as well as &quot;to save my friend's life, I must murder/kidnap their child.&quot; Good stuff.<br /> <br /> 2. Heaven has no policy, but the Sids &quot;police&quot; themselves. In some cases, dark, horrible things happen to children of Sidereals who choose to have them. If you want an especially dark take, operatives tend to only find this out the hard way.<br /> <br /> Or, if you like your Exalted with less grimdark:<br /> 1. At some point, lots of Sids make babies. It just kinda happens. Off the books, there is a village in Creation for the mortal(ish) children and spouses of the Maidens' Chosen. Fate always ensures this town enjoys great, if boring, fortune. Marauding armies miss it. Expanding empires never add it to their maps. Fair Folk who try to raid it find an increasingly improbable amount of opposition and happenstance turning against them. It's accepted between all factions that this place is simply neutral. But what happens when someone decides to break that truce?<br /> <br /> 2. Heavens' gods, not really understanding the nuances of human reproduction, and the utter helplessness of children, just assume the Sidereal can take it along with them. There are no policies, no daycare, no maternity leave. Just...figure it out. Shenanigans ensue.<br /> <br /> 3. Sids just never have kids. This departs from canon, but it could be interesting. Somewhere along the way, someone built into the Loom that it never happens. Until it happens to a PC.<br /> <br /> And if you like things light-hearted and kinda funny.<br /> 1. Sidereal children reflect the Caste of their parents, ensuring that whatever the Sid brings to Creation, they will find at home (Even Serenity can be a bad thing when it's your teen that's into it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T05:30:16-07:00","id":631056,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;If it wouldn't be too much trouble, could we catch a boat to Port Calin?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Princes of the Earth looked at their travelling companion a little oddly. Rarely did he voice an opinion on where they headed or even what was for dinner any given night. He gave them a sheepish grin and elaborated &quot;I've got a little family business that I need to tend to.&quot; He hefted his backpack a bit further up on his shoulder.</i><i>Ledaal</i><i>Solfiru</i><i> smiles reassuringly at him, having taken a liking to the introverted young man. </i><i>Sesus</i><i> Darthak furrowed his brow skeptically. While the companion was decent in a fight, he wanted to know fully what they were getting into, ans asked for an elaboration of &quot;business.&quot;<br /> <br /> The young man retrieved a small package from his backpack and re-read the note one more time. &quot;On the 18th day of resplendent air I am to hang a blue curtain in a particular apartment before the sun rises.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i>Solofiru</i><i> smiled bemusedly and said &quot;I've been wanting to visit a </i><i>Calinite</i><i> tailor...we can make time for...whatever business you have.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> When we had players portray Star-blessed, it was often as minor functionaries who sometimes did things that they didn't fully understand but just shrugged and carried out. One notable character traipsed across creation to secure signatures from other sideral s for their parent. He didn't really know that was what he was doing, but more or less.<br /> <br /> They were armed with kung-fu (including celestial styles), the occasional Sidereal charm (heavily restricted access), and a good deal of luck and an interesting sense of adventure.<br /> <br /> As a result, I'm very fond of star-blessed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/999-winterstar","name":"Winterstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar999_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T05:53:31-07:00","id":631074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=631049#post631049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of Sids, they may be called upon to bring about the genocide of their personal dynasty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder... when you live for thousands of years, how distantly descended is somebody liable to be before you stop really feeling any sense of kinship with them?<br /> <br /> The term &quot;personal dynasty&quot; gives me the image of a family group that has specifically built itself around a set of imagery based on a noteworthy common ancestor or group identity, which I can see as a thing of some frequency for Solars and Lunars and maybe an occasional thing for Sidereals (and of course, something that the most powerful Dragon Blooded of the Age of Sorrows built themselves around), but it's not necessarily comprehensive.<br /> <br /> I can see a Sidereal as taking issue with one of their children or even grandchildren being caught up in some impending disaster (and would say that, in the majority of cases, it's as simple as just arranging their relocation ahead of time; I don't think the plans of Heaven often call for specific individuals to be hit by something), but a descendent separated by a few hundred years... do you care? Do you feel any more sense of familial connection to them than to any other random person, who for all intents and purposes (and genetic examination) is just as closely related to you?<br /> <br /> Not to mention how Sidereals aren't being called on to oversee historical troubles or human disasters all the time.<br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is that I don't think a Sidereal happening to have a child is typically going to be much of a disaster.<br /> <br /> That idea of <u>happening</u> to have one or more is key to my thinking, by the way. I think Sidereals are unlikely to wind up having many mortal children because the opportunities don't come up very frequently.<br /> <br /> I feel as though some of the ideas in this thread might emerge from a fairly modern and somewhat middle class perspective on having children; something that you <i>decide</i> to do and even put a bit of deliberate effort towards. Even disregarding attitudes towards contraception (even if it's become fairly ubiquitous and effective in the modern day), I think a lot of the kinds of people who are in a position to decide to have children are ones whose relationship has assumed that state of sex being comfortably infrequent, so part of the decision entails increasing its frequency.<br /> <br /> I think that historically, children were just assumed to be something that just happened as a result of marriage. Not as a matter of people being ignorant of the causation, just... they'd have sex with whatever frequency, and conception would happen when it happened. Part of that attitude that viewed children as little blessings.<br /> <br /> (I know it's outright different for some groups in the setting, especially the Scarlet Dynasty, but they've got their own reasons)<br /> <br /> The point of all this is me suggesting that if you're a Sidereal, you probably don't often have the attitude that having a child is something you decide to do (even if they have powers for it and can often be the actual source of that blessing for other people), and you're not often part of the relationship in which it's just going to arise naturally from a long enough time span, so... it doesn't really seem like an important enough thing to be made a big deal of. If it happens, how it's dealt with is largely in the hands of the Sidereal it happens to. I think in most cases that would amount to sending them a few pleasant destinies, maybe visiting on occasion, and otherwise being a non-entity in their life. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T06:01:43-07:00","id":631092,"title":"","content":"I'll admit I'm borrowing somewhat from the ideas of V;tM, where essentially immortal people with great power sometimes invest heavily in their descendants kn order to feel a connection to something. I can see it happening to Sids. After a few centuries of watching but never doing, it's easy to yearn for something human. It might not matter for all of them, but for some, certainly.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't think it's safe to assume that Sids don't get it on fairly regularly. As I put it to my noobie players last time we played &quot;Sex in Creation is a form of recreation, like video games or watching a movie.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T06:20:06-07:00","id":631098,"title":"","content":"This is at least one reason to have a firmer sense of what Sidereal action in the setting is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sex in Creation is a form of recreation, like video games or watching a movie.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Are you sure that's not masturbation? (And also that that isn't the exact same attitude as in real life)</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T06:36:15-07:00","id":631104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=631098#post631098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And also that that isn't the exact same attitude as in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the electricity goes out, people get bored. <br /> <br /> (So many hurricane babies....) <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T06:58:22-07:00","id":631126,"title":"","content":"I meant more about the masturbation.<br /> <br /> Sex is something that necessarily requires an interested partner, so it can't <i>quite</i> be something that people treat recreationally (even if the majority of people in Creation aren't divided into categories of &quot;has to do physically intensive labour most of the time&quot; and &quot;is part of a social stratum in which all actions and relationships are very heavily scrutinised&quot;).<br /> <br /> I get that the <i>books</i> more frequently note the sexual relationships of characters, but I don't think the setting is one in which people are notably more sexually open (indeed, a lot of the times when the books bring up people's relationships, they still seem to be somewhat discrete about it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T07:18:56-07:00","id":631152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=631126#post631126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that the <i>books</i> more frequently note the sexual relationships of characters, but I don't think the setting is one in which people are notably more sexually open (indeed, a lot of the times when the books bring up people's relationships, they still seem to be somewhat discrete about it).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure I've seen notes/comments from Grabowksi and Moran to the effect that Creation is intended to be more open about sex, which makes me think that the above, as with many other problems in presentation, have been from writers not understanding the setting.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T07:24:43-07:00","id":631157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=631152#post631152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure I've seen notes/comments from Grabowksi and Moran to the effect that Creation is intended to be more open about sex, which makes me think that the above, as with many other problems in presentation, have been from writers not understanding the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I get some sources? I'd like to hear more about this.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T07:36:48-07:00","id":631166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=631157#post631157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I get some sources? I'd like to hear more about this.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll see what I can dig up during my lunch break in a couple hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T08:09:19-07:00","id":631191,"title":"","content":"Does that mean more open about sex in the sense of not having a (for want of a better word) puritan kind of mindset in which it's publicly considered something kind of shameful and unfortunately necessary and something to deride anybody who is openly known to engage in it, or something like, maybe the Kinsey institute or the characters of Sex and the City?<br /> <br /> I think one can have something like people being generally aware of Ragara Banobas being engaged in a relationship without his boyfriend being somebody who outright discusses their sex life with his friends over drinks or something.<br /> <br /> Or the idea that there's nothing sordid or secret about characters who hit it off in some kind of public forum like a sporting event or place to get alcohol and go off somewhere private together, but stopping short of... I don't know, the idea that people are frequent about openly and earnestly looking for sex from people (I feel this is probably strawmanning a bit, so I'm going to ask what the terms of any given image of &quot;Creation as sexually open&quot; might be).<br /> <br /> Notwithstanding the presentation of cultures such as An-Teng, mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T09:05:31-07:00","id":631247,"title":"","content":"Even if they don't commonly form long-term relationships with mortals, Sidereals are still human, and as a group probably have the same average sex drive as any other humans. They're going to find sexual partners or do plenty of masturbating. They're going to crave actual relationships with people who can remember them, be they Celestial gods or fellow Sidereals or something else. I get that their aloofness and detachment from humanity is one of their worst flaws, and think it's in-theme for them to get eccentric and callous from being denied the basics of human community that nearly everybody else has, but many or most will find ways to have sex, even if it's just a prostitute in some town they're passing through, or a brief fling with a coworker. Unless you want to say their society enforces vows of celibacy on the level of the Immaculate Order or the Catholic priesthood, but I think that's rather doubtful -- canonically we know some have long-term lovers, such as Chejop and Ayesha.<br /> <br /> They're going to notice that babies sometimes happen, and <i><b>if</b></i> that's something that bothers them, they can easily afford maiden tea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=630930#post630930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that's what Life Without Compunction is for!</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that really enough to prevent a Romeo and Juliet situation from exploding the day after the Sidereal matchmaker leaves town? If a Sidereal is directed to breed two families together (for a political alliance, or to increase the Dragons' Blood, or because their descendants will enable the Division to do X in regards to local destiny, or prevent some other match) and those two families hate each other, a wise Sidereal will arrange things in a way that either socially legitimizes the match, or removes the couple from the gaze of their disapproving society (if that doesn't go against the whole plan). Removing them may mean physically sending them out of the country, removing their relatives' power to sanction/kill them, hiding the ancestry of one or both partners like Lady Jessica in Dune, or making the liason entirely secret.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-18-2015, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T10:36:37-07:00","id":631301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=631152#post631152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure I've seen notes/comments from Grabowksi and Moran to the effect that Creation is intended to be more open about sex, which makes me think that the above, as with many other problems in presentation, have been from writers not understanding the setting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is probably more open than you'd expect from, say, the medieval world (although the medieval world was more open than many people think, since it was pre-puritan), but that doesn't necessarily mean people are <i>having</i> lots more sex, because most people still can't afford effective contraception, if they even know much about effective contraception. People probably don't slut-shame so much, but most young women are probably not sleeping with as many men as they can because that means they'll get knocked up.<br /> I'd imagine (and I think this was the intention) its somewhat similar to the west in the modern day. Yes, we don't have Victorian attitudes. That doesn't mean everyone's screwing everyone all the time. A lot of people would still prefer to stick with their husband or wife, even if society wouldn't ostracise them for not doing so.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine Sidereal women may or may not take lovers, but if they do, they generally use maiden tea because they can afford it and they're too overworked to have kids. The men probably vary depending on how jaded they are about mortals (I'd imagine a lot of older Sidereals are extremely jaded about mortals). It probably varies a lot. A few probably sow bastards all over the place, but most probably don't.<br /> The only time they're likely to raise a child, however, is if its with another Sidereal or a god. Raising kids with a mortal is difficult because of a)arcane fate, b)working in Yu-Shan, and c)being an immortal who'll outlive your kids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-18-2015, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T20:06:04-07:00","id":631838,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=631049#post631049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading over all this, it strikes me that Heaven wouldn't really want Sidereals to have connections like children. Sids are expected to be able to allow (or force) the massacre of entire cities, to preside over the death-pangs of empires. if you go with the 2E interpretation, that included literally planning human history on a large scale (hope that gets changed).<br /> <br /> People who make those kinds of decisions don't really benefit from having kids. It's one thing when you are a leader in your own nation. Then making your nation powerful helps protect your kids. In the case of Sids, they may be called upon to bring about the genocide of their personal dynasty. In the real world, we call that a potential conflict of interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, the way they've been described so far, they don't just blindly follow a script, they just have a much better idea of what cause will end up with what effect. It seems unlikely that fate demands the death of a group of people without any alternatives - sure, the Sid's family may live in Gem, but there should be no problem with &quot;some&quot; people escaping its inevitable destruction. And if fate really &quot;demands&quot; the death of the Sid's family? Admin access to the Loom of Fate. They pull a few favours, and that destiny is now some mortal family's problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=631049#post631049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like really good story fodder to me. You can play it one of a few ways.<br /> 1. Heaven has directives specifically forbidding anyone working with the Bureau of Destiny from reproducing. In the event they do, the child is killed/taken away. Lots of interesting &quot;going rogue to save my kid&quot; stories there, as well as &quot;to save my friend's life, I must murder/kidnap their child.&quot; Good stuff.<br /> <br /> 2. Heaven has no policy, but the Sids &quot;police&quot; themselves. In some cases, dark, horrible things happen to children of Sidereals who choose to have them. If you want an especially dark take, operatives tend to only find this out the hard way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because those are <i>great ways</i> to inspire loyalty, and Sidereals always blindly follow orders. Nah, I'd expect this to end up in a heavenly civil war, and Rakan Thulio would be just one of many sids declaring war on heaven.<br /> <br /> I'd be on board with Yu Shan prohibiting children (since Sids are supposed to be impartial), but this is <i>Yu Shan</i> we're talking about. At worst, having children should be a severety [something] offense - it might get the Sid into trouble, but it's nothing they couldn't get out of again. It's not like Fate was this big, immutable constant. Sids rewrite it all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T11:26:15-07:00","id":632555,"title":"","content":"Ha, impartial. Yeah, right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T11:31:36-07:00","id":632559,"title":"","content":"I don't want there to be a whole splat where having children is illegal. At the worse, Kejak should be mumbling &quot;Haven't these people heard of Maiden Tea?&quot; when he gets a maternity/paternity sabbatical request.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T13:22:45-07:00","id":632688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=632555#post632555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ha, impartial. Yeah, right.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Supposed</i> to be, but then - I'm not sure, is 3ed still going to have the &quot;Everyone is overworked and no one has the time to follow the rules&quot;-theme for Yu Shan? I mean, IIRC, in 2ed you could brush of most audits (if it even ever got to one) with a simple dice throw.<br /> <br /> That's why I'd be okay with this level of &quot;prohibition&quot; - it might be something that's brought up if someone tries to harm the Sid's career (since it'd be technically illegal), but it's not something that anyone would bother to enforce on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T13:59:58-07:00","id":632704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=632688#post632688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Supposed</i> to be, but then - I'm not sure, is 3ed still going to have the &quot;Everyone is overworked and no one has the time to follow the rules&quot;-theme for Yu Shan?</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be too early to say, as yet. For now, here's what we've heard:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sids are going to be restored to their awesome position of beneficiary service, where they are respected by the gods. However, we love the corrupt, dangerous side of Yu-Shan so we are playing that up.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T20:57:16-07:00","id":633011,"title":"","content":"I meant that if they gave a fart about impartiality (or their real job) there would be no factions. If there are rules against having kids to prevent bias, most likely nobody cares about them except the few independents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-20-2015, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T02:02:25-07:00","id":633303,"title":"","content":"I feel like I should say that I'm still reading this thread. Right now, I'm just sitting here drinking my coffee, absolutely <i>fascinated </i>by where this topic went. Going back to what was said earlier, I can see where Isator Levi is coming from, but it strikes me that there's two ways of looking at a Sidereal -- is the archetypal Chosen of the Maidens a glorious magical vizier who weaves webs intricate enough to catch gods and mortals, and finds it unnecessary to stoop to tricks when they're granted the power and oversight of heaven; or is the archetypal Sidereal a glorious, powerful being hampered at every turn by bureaucracy of Heaven, the seeming indifference of the Maidens, having to inefficiently deal with the responsibilities originally held by four groups of Exalted, and by the reality of only 100 Sidereals being responsible for literally millions of miles of Creation?<br /> <br /> I think Exalted is big enough for both interpretations, but they do change the way a Sidereal interacts with the everyday world of Creation. With the former interpretation, no, it wouldn't be reasonable to expect a Sidereal to &quot;play mortal&quot;, since they don't <i>have</i> to. Plots and actors revolve around a Sidereal, not the other way around. And anyone who disagrees with that gets transfortuned into being a dung-heaper or gets shot with an arrow made of the sensation of a summer breeze. But given the latter interpretation, one has to imagine that every assignment that a hypothetical Sidereal takes in Creation fills them with a chronic, low-level anxiety. They have the weight of expectation on their shoulders, and every action comes with questions: &quot;What if I make a mistake and get a Wyld Hunt coming after me?&quot;, &quot;What if I screw up with my charms and have to report to eight different bureaus when I get back to Yu-Shan?&quot;, &quot;What if I play with astrology too much and a Pattern Spider feels that the best way to resolve that problem is to bite me in the throat?&quot; You have to imagine that in that case, a Sidereal would be slightly desperate to stay under the supernatural radar and rely on mundane and possibly amoral methods of solving problems; methods such as larceny, murder, and -- fitting this topic -- creating children for a socio-political purpose.<br /> <br /> It boils down to whether your story demands the Sidereals who are mythical figures of puissance and absolute dignity, or the Sidereals who are overworked, exhausted middlemen whose attempts to repair cracks in Creation are met with a half-dozen more cracks showing up the moment they finish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T03:06:31-07:00","id":633314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=633303#post633303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It boils down to whether your story demands the Sidereals who are mythical figures of puissance and absolute dignity, or the Sidereals who are overworked, exhausted middlemen whose attempts to repair cracks in Creation are met with a half-dozen more cracks showing up the moment they finish.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;or&quot; is unnecessary.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T04:04:56-07:00","id":633323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=633303#post633303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But given the latter interpretation, one has to imagine that every assignment that a hypothetical Sidereal takes in Creation fills them with a chronic, low-level anxiety. They have the weight of expectation on their shoulders, and every action comes with questions: &quot;What if I make a mistake and get a Wyld Hunt coming after me?&quot;, &quot;What if I screw up with my charms and have to report to eight different bureaus when I get back to Yu-Shan?&quot;, &quot;What if I play with astrology too much and a Pattern Spider feels that the best way to resolve that problem is to bite me in the throat?&quot; You have to imagine that in that case, a Sidereal would be slightly desperate to stay under the supernatural radar and rely on mundane and possibly amoral methods of solving problems; methods such as larceny, murder, and -- fitting this topic -- creating children for a socio-political purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals have gotten a pretty raw deal so far, so any interpretation that involves them not using their charms etc. doesn't work.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that challenges resulting from red tape or corruption shouldn't be played or aren't interesting. Another bureau directly opposes the goal of your mission but won't consider budging until they meet again three weeks too late for your assignment. Then you get to decide whether you'd like to provoke their wrath or try to subtly work around their restrictions. OK, great fun, very Sidereal. But if Sidereals face all the Wyld Hunt worries that Solars etc. do plus a bunch of heavenly nut-kicking, that's cruel. It's also too much of that 2e, &quot;Everyone in Yu-Shan knows every time a Sid uses any kind of magic, and they all try to come up with ways to nut-kick the Sids for it.&quot; A Heaven in need of reform and repair is interesting, but not one that's characterized by comical bed-shitting self-hatred.<br /> <br /> Also for real nothing justifies having a kid except needing to have a kid, specifically, yourself. And the more overworked the Sidereal is, the less it makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T06:25:46-07:00","id":633379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=633314#post633314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;or&quot; is unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the story of the blind men and the elephant, it all depends on which side you're examining.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Originally posted by <b>Root</b><br /> <br /> Sidereals have gotten a pretty raw deal so far, so any interpretation that involves them not using their charms etc. doesn't work.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that challenges resulting from red tape or corruption shouldn't be played or aren't interesting. Another bureau directly opposes the goal of your mission but won't consider budging until they meet again three weeks too late for your assignment. Then you get to decide whether you'd like to provoke their wrath or try to subtly work around their restrictions. OK, great fun, very Sidereal. But if Sidereals face all the Wyld Hunt worries that Solars etc. do plus a bunch of heavenly nut-kicking, that's cruel. It's also too much of that 2e, &quot;Everyone in Yu-Shan knows every time a Sid uses any kind of magic, and they all try to come up with ways to nut-kick the Sids for it.&quot; A Heaven in need of reform and repair is interesting, but not one that's characterized by comical bed-shitting self-hatred.<br /> <br /> Also for real nothing justifies having a kid except needing to have a kid, specifically, yourself. And the more overworked the Sidereal is, the less it makes sense. </div> </div> </div>I get this feeling that people think that I'm insisting on &quot;Sidereals all gotta get pregnant!&quot; On the contrary, I more or less agree with what's been said in previous posts -- I imagine that Sidereals have plenty of reasons to avoid getting entangled with mortal destinies more than necessary. Still, I do think it's a narratively fascinating premise for a handful of the grand plotweavers of Yu-Shan to have children with mortals. It could speak to the callous pragmatism of a Sidereal creating a life just to sacrifice it for the sake of an assignment. It could speak to the humanity of a Sidereal developing a sense of regret about doing that very thing. Whether or not it would actually be valid is up to you, but it's not something I pulled out of the ether -- it's pretty common to the &quot;evil vizier&quot; trope that inspired the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Also, I wasn't necessarily limiting the problems Sidereals face to &quot;interference from Yu-Shan&quot;. Let's say a Sidereal had a long-term assignment in one location. They could spend Personal Essence doing subtle and non-obvious charms, but what happens weeks down the line when they need to start drawing from Peripheral Essence, or the supernatural solution for a problem requires an obvious charm? I mean, Arcane Fate is powerful, but it's not going to save a Sidereal's bacon when they start glowing blue and a big, glowing mirror symbol shows up on their forehead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T07:07:37-07:00","id":633400,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Wyld Hunt specifically, I don't care for the 2E notion that everything with a caste mark counts as Anathema. I think even the Bronzes had enough sense to limit the definition of Anathema specifically to Solars and Lunars, and in 3E that'll be specifically true. A dude who glows blue with a strange forehead mark is a weird and possibly dangerous supernatural that merits investigation, and that'll inconvenience them, but it's silly for Immaculates to consider them Anathema.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, I prefer both of those interpretations to be true at the same time. They are overwhelmed because Creation is dying, the gods and other Exalted are no longer doing their jobs (mostly thanks to the Sidereals' own mistakes), the Sidereals are wasting insane amounts of time and resources on political/faction BS, and the Incarnae don't care. They're also Exalted with all that should imply about dignity and being designed to be capable of doing the job they were designed for, even during a crisis as extreme as the Primordial War.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Regarding whether there should be a Bureau rule against having children... aside from the question of whether such a rule would be necessary or important (I don't think so) there are thematic and narrative questions about it.<br /> <br /> 1. Thematically: if one of the themes of Yu-Shan is bureaucratic corruption and red tape, which fits better? A blanket (straightforward, easily understood) &quot;no children&quot; rule, or a bunch of needlessly convoluted extra forms and hoops you have to jump through and confusing rules about where and when and how you may have children and who you have to notify?<br /> <br /> 2. Narratively: Would such a rule serve to enhance the experience of playing Sidereals? The idea of having kids tugs at major narrative tensions in their lives. Is your PC a callous manipulator who uses and sacrifices anyone, even their closest kin and friends? Or are they trying to balance their duties and cynical environment with a more caring, humanistic/humane attitude? Is your PC detatched from humans and their own personal humanity, or do they struggle to find ways to affirm their humanity and human connections in spite of Arcane Fate? Do they confine themselves to meaningful social interaction within Yu-Shan, or do they try to have real [ish] relationships with Creationionites? How do you possibly find enough time in your day for all the stuff you have to do, and do you make extra time to care for your kid or foster them on somebody else? I think it's important to ask whether a &quot;no children&quot; rule would get in the way of dealing with those tensions in regards to romance, sexuality, and reproduction, or if it would enhance the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-20-2015, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T07:11:59-07:00","id":633406,"title":"","content":"A Sidereal with anima showing will probably be mistaken for an Exigent in Ex3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T19:08:51-07:00","id":634154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=633400#post633400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Wyld Hunt specifically, I don't care for the 2E notion that everything with a caste mark counts as Anathema. I think even the Bronzes had enough sense to limit the definition of Anathema specifically to Solars and Lunars, and in 3E that'll be specifically true. A dude who glows blue with a strange forehead mark is a weird and possibly dangerous supernatural that merits investigation, and that'll inconvenience them, but it's silly for Immaculates to consider them Anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like the &quot;Sidereals as Anathema&quot; thing, if only because it really fits with the Sidereals' theme of scheming that comes back to bite them in their collective ass. They broke the Mask to usurp the Solars. They created the Immaculate faith to reinforce the political legitimacy of Terrestrial rule and to keep the Lunars and Solars at bay. But those two plots ran into each other -- by breaking the Mask and retreating to Yu-Shan, almost nobody knows that the Sidereals exist. By creating the Immaculate doctrine that Exalted are defined by Anima Flux, they made caste marks a symbol of demonic Anathema. Since most people -- Terrestrials included -- don't know that the Sidereals exist, they're going to turn to Immaculate doctrine that a big, glowing forehead mark signifies a powerful and evil tempter to be immediately destroyed. Most people in Creation aren't going to look at a Sidereal caste mark and stick around to compare the differences between a Chosen of Mars' caste mark and the mark of one of the &quot;Wretched&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals only have two options to <i>not</i> be Anathema, and both options are potentially worse than the current status quo:<br /> <br /> 1. They repair the Mask and return to Creation. This has the effect of shaking the very core of the Immaculate faith, the legitimacy of Terrestrial rulership, and raises uncomfortable questions in both Creation and Yu-Shan about the Usurpation, sparking civil wars in both Creation and Heaven.<br /> <br /> 2. They retreat completely from Creation and avoid the risk of their members being labeled Anathema in the first place. This has the effect of one of Creation's few remaining protector-overseers no longer being able to solve problems on the ground. The stability of the world begins to fall apart as civil wars, revolts, and supernatural threats start growing faster than Creation's other forces of stability can quash them.<br /> <br /> Will the arrival of the Liminals, Getimians, and Exigents change this? Maybe. But based on the current narrative, the Sidereals shot themselves in the foot by creating the definition of Anathema, and they can't solve that problem without causing Heaven and Creation to explode in civil disorder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","user":"Kallipolis","date":". 08-20-2015, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T21:56:02-07:00","id":634250,"title":"","content":"Actually, Kal, they created the Immaculate <i>Order</i> and the Immaculate <i>Philosophy</i>. The Immaculate Faith was established when Lookshy refused to follow the Immaculate Order in legitimizing the Scarlet Empress' rule. Sidereals has no hand in its making.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T03:43:06-07:00","id":634430,"title":"","content":"I think it's more like &quot;Sidereals establish Immaculate Philosophy, it spreads throughout the Shogunate, and then when Chejop made the alliance with the Empress they refined the dogma within the Realm into the form that outright endorses Dragon Blooded supremacy&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate practices in Lookshy are apparently closer to what it was like in the Shogunate, which was still made by the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Even if the Sidereals don't directly control it (because it doesn't actually have a hierarchy), it probably still benefits them to have the second major grouping of Terrestrials adhere to ideals and rituals of restraint and responsibility which were the whole point of the Philosophy in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T05:25:33-07:00","id":634467,"title":"","content":"My point is more that the last seven hundred plus years of ideology of the IO (<i>and</i> the Bronze Faction!) involves legitimizing the Empress' rule, to better lend her empire stability; the Bronze Sidereals had as much of a hand establishing the Immaculate Faith as Jesus did establishing the Eastern Orthodox Church.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T14:02:29-07:00","id":635051,"title":"","content":"Well, I think most Orthodox Bishops would argue Jesus did, in fact, establish the Eastern Orthodox Church... That's actually an important part of their doctrinal claims to authority (as with the Catholic Church).<br /> <br /> Probably more comparable would be... I can't think of a perfect comparison. As much of a hand establishing the Immaculate Faith as the Bishops of Rome?<br /> This is probably not very important to the main point you're making, but anyhow.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T14:30:41-07:00","id":635072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Bronze Sidereals had as much of a hand establishing the Immaculate Faith as Jesus did establishing the Eastern Orthodox Church.</div> </div> </div> </div> I find this analogy to be mistaken. I think the image of the Immaculates you're presenting would be more akin to saying that the founding of Mormonism imposed a state of being founded anew on all non-Mormon churches, which also suddenly have nothing to do with Jesus. Really, the Immaculates and Sidereals are more like any occasion in which somebody founds a political party, gradually becomes disillusioned with it, and then joins a breakaway group as leader again while the former party continues to exist. An occasion in which the breakaway happens to actually take most of the members. I call this effect &quot;Sinn Fein&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T00:41:02-07:00","id":635492,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, not sure it's really being disillusioned. The Sidereals started one thing, then turned it into another form, while a few die-hards claimed to be following the old form (but weren't quite). Maybe like &quot;Socialist Labour&quot; in Britain: a tiny group that claimed to be keeping the &quot;Old Labour&quot; flame alive, while Labour had become New Labour.<br /> I don't know enough about Irish politics to think of an equivalent example.<br /> Maybe... Protestantism in Ulster? Protestantism was the religion of the ruling class of Anglo-Irish nobles. But then suddenly all these guys with a newer, even less Catholic version of Protestantism turned up, and so the old Protestant nobles found themselves siding with the Catholics against the Imperial power and the Presbyterians who supported it.<br /> <br /> Maybe this search for an apt simile is just doomed to failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T02:10:50-07:00","id":635521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know enough about Irish politics to think of an equivalent example.</div> </div> </div> </div> Once there was Sinn F\u00e9in, the Republican party, that after the Easter Rising was filled up with all the disaffected elements of the country (including many former Home Rulers, which left <i>that</i> party a rump of what it once was). It came under the leadership of one Eamon de Valera. Then the whole civil war thing happened, and the party split into two, with the... more respectable side becoming the party that we call Fine Gael today, and the other side still Sinn F\u00e9in, who abstained from political participation and continued to associate with the IRA; de Valera took their side. Eventually, de Valera became distressed by the violence of the IRA and the increasingly apparent uselessness of a party that wouldn't take part in politics, and when his suggestion that they end abstention was rejected by the IRA elements, he left the Sinn F\u00e9in name and took the majority of the party with him; the party he founded out of them also had the name of the Republican party, as it still advocated for many of the same things (particularly an Irish republic). In the modern Republic, Sinn F\u00e9in still exists, still advocates for the integration of Northern Ireland (among other issues), and has a direct line of continuity to the party that de Valera led, but is a lot smaller than the new one he made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T02:37:18-07:00","id":635535,"title":"","content":"I knew about the pre-independence politics (the Home Rule party and so on), and a bit about Sinn Fein (from the Northern Irish perspective), but I didn't know that Fine Gael had come from Sinn Fein. I also assumed that most of the Irish parties still advocated unification vaguely, they just didn't ever do anything about it or expect it to ever happen (the way, say, Plaid Cymru officially advocates Welsh independence, but they don't ever do anything about it, and if you ask them seriously they'll admit it's never going to happen; but it's still their official aim).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T04:08:47-07:00","id":635577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't know that Fine Gael had come from Sinn Fein.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's actually kind of interesting to note how if there hadn't been a civil war, the country would technically have been a single-party state. In the first election of a technically legal Irish parliament, a lot of Sinn Fein candidates ran unopposed; it just happened that there was a foundational issue they were divided over. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also assumed that most of the Irish parties still advocated unification vaguely, they just didn't ever do anything about it or expect it to ever happen</div> </div> </div> </div> Basically, although a lot more active work is put towards forms of conciliation. But I digress too much, I'll leave this topic now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T04:48:00-07:00","id":635601,"title":"","content":"Well, it's always interesting to learn about other country's political parties.<br /> The country I live in has a political party that most of the people don't even really understand, including my friend who's a party secretary for our department. When I ask my students they mostly go &quot;oh, we sleep through our politics lessons.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyhow, back to Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-22-2015, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T17:20:01-07:00","id":638497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=632559#post632559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want there to be a whole splat where having children is illegal. At the worse, Kejak should be mumbling &quot;Haven't these people heard of Maiden Tea?&quot; when he gets a maternity/paternity sabbatical request.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm not sure why this point is still in discussion. Sidereals are still kinda human, so human things\u2014like wanting to have a family\u2014are likely still going to be there. Part of having a family is having kids, either through the regular means or adoption, so why wouldn't some Sidereals have children? Granted, their jobs and the way Arcane Fate works makes it much harder, but that also lends itself to interesting stories. I can certainly see stories of Sidereals that have a child and lose contact with it because of those two factors, vowing never again to subject themselves to such pain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=633400#post633400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Wyld Hunt specifically, I don't care for the 2E notion that everything with a caste mark counts as Anathema. I think even the Bronzes had enough sense to limit the definition of Anathema specifically to Solars and Lunars, and in 3E that'll be specifically true. A dude who glows blue with a strange forehead mark is a weird and possibly dangerous supernatural that merits investigation, and that'll inconvenience them, but it's silly for Immaculates to consider them Anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the distinction that the Solars, Lunars and Sidereals have regarding the fact that their caste marks appear on the forehead, and the lack of such marks from other supernatural beings, I can see how at least some Immaculates would be quick to label such beings as &quot;Anethema&quot; or possibly Anethema-touched. There would likely be similar reactions to Green Sun Princes\u2014probably even stronger, since they tend to have more obvious demon-touched features.<br /> <br /> That being said, there's likely nothing in the text refering to the Maidens regarding what is considered Anethema, which an astute study of the text would likely know (which is something wonderandawe also played with in her hero quest).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5492-xeno426","name":"Xeno426","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5492_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T19:23:48-07:00","id":638693,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing the average <i><b>peasant</b></i> freaks out at weird glowy things, no matter what color they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T19:32:39-07:00","id":638703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=638693#post638693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing the average <i><b>peasant</b></i> freaks out at weird glowy things, no matter what color they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. The average peasant doesn't get to see much of any anima banner, even Dragonblooded. And once they do, they probably head for the storm cellar until the demigods finish whatever they are doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T19:33:20-07:00","id":638706,"title":"","content":"The average peasant probably knows, at least from stories, what the local gods look like and what their Exalted masters look like when they exhibit their power. Similarly, they've heard instruction on the Fair Folk, demons, and the worst of all, the silver and (much rarer) golden Anathema.<br /> <br /> Other woogidy supernatural stuff probably provokes a reaction of &quot;get away and find a priest.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T19:44:42-07:00","id":638710,"title":"","content":"Considering that Anathema look like specific things, but spirits and faeries can look like anything, &quot;some kinda god or demon or fae&quot; is probably the default assumption when a Sidereal shows themselves. They go run find a priest, the Sidereal hides, the priest comes back and asks &quot;Where is this spirit?&quot; and everybody goes &quot;What? I dunno.&quot; Inconvenient, but not often life-threatening.<br /> <br /> Getting hoist by their own petard would be a fitting (if totally inadequate) punishment for breaking the sky and genociding random non-Exalts all over the world, but it just isn't plausible to me that they'd have written the dogma that way. Now, if Kejak and his cronies had pissed off the Empress enough that she decided she had to cut ties with Sidereals in the earliest years of the Realm and the Immaculate Order, she probably could have arranged for Sidereals to be Anathema according to the Order. And it would've been <b><i>hilarious</i></b>. But, she didn't.<br /> <br /> I suppose one could justify it with a headcanon that the early Shogunate Dragon-Blooded who started the Immaculate Philosophy resented and distrusted Sidereal manipulation so much that they decided to redefine Anathema as &quot;everything with a caste mark and anima.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-24-2015, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T19:50:33-07:00","id":638714,"title":"","content":"In 3.0, I expect when someone spots a Sid, the assumption is that they're an Exigent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T20:24:04-07:00","id":638732,"title":"","content":"I suspect that the higher-order Immaculates, the upper crust of the Realm aristocracy, and the learned would be able to judge the factors that distinguish &quot;Anathema&quot; from other phenomena in Creation (and outside of it). But for the country priests, peasantry, and common labor that makes up the lion's share of Creation society, would they have the knowledge to distinguish between the different Exalted, the fae, and other mysterious beings?<br /> <br /> I mean, would French peasants in the 13th century be able to distinguish between miaphysitism and Arianism as two specific and mutually-exclusive theological branches of Christian belief? It'd all be &quot;heresy&quot; -- and therefore &quot;dangerous&quot; -- to them, and to be reported to an authority as soon as possible.<br /> <br /> Now, the Exigents are going to shift the categories a little bit, but <i>in general</i>, I think that 90+% of the population of Creation would see a Sidereal caste mark and not sit around to ask questions about its provenience. And I think that's perfectly fine for Exalted's narrative. The hubris of the Sidereals screwed them over, and now they have to deal with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T20:56:48-07:00","id":638772,"title":"","content":"I expect the average person within the Immaculate Philosophy's sphere of influence knows what a Lunar looks like. &quot;Glows silver,&quot; &quot;can steal people's faces,&quot; &quot;can transform into animals,&quot; and &quot;has moon symbols on forehead&quot; aren't superhard to understand.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T21:34:38-07:00","id":638797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=638772#post638772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect the average person within the Immaculate Philosophy's sphere of influence knows what a Lunar looks like. &quot;Glows silver,&quot; &quot;can steal people's faces,&quot; &quot;can transform into animals,&quot; and &quot;has moon symbols on forehead&quot; aren't superhard to understand.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but what's the immediate difference between a No Moon Caste's, Night Caste's, Day Caste's, and Chosen of Mars' caste marks to an unlettered and terrified peasant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T22:44:19-07:00","id":638823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=638797#post638797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe, but what's the immediate difference between a No Moon Caste's, Night Caste's, Day Caste's, and Chosen of Mars' caste marks to an unlettered and terrified peasant?</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the difference between silver, gold, a bleeding wound and red?<br /> <br /> edit: unless the question is about what it means to see one, in which case there is no difference; all of those mean &quot;run&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7103-owill0w","user":"Owill0w","date":". 08-25-2015, 02:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7103-owill0w","name":"Owill0w","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T23:43:18-07:00","id":638852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Owill0w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=638823#post638823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the difference between silver, gold, a bleeding wound and red?<br /> <br /> edit: unless the question is about what it means to see one, in which case there is no difference; all of those mean &quot;run&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a sense. If a Creation peasant, educated only in harvesting rice and whatever is taught by the local Immaculate priest, sees a glowing circle on a stranger's forehead, swirling with light and whorls of Essence, what would be the <i>immediate</i> difference to them? I mean, yes, there are slight qualitative differences, but given a quick glance (and that's all a peasant would spare before legging it), they're extremely similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6872-kallipolis","name":"Kallipolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T08:00:35-07:00","id":639098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=638714#post638714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 3.0, I expect when someone spots a Sid, the assumption is that they're an Exigent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect the average person doesn't know what an Exigent is, and lumps all Exigents, Sidereals, Getimians, Liminals, and Green Sun Princes into &quot;Weird glowy thing, probably a dangerous spirit, run away and find a priest/monk/exorcist.&quot; Exigents aren't a group with any unifying characteristics aside from their origins, they've been on the decline since the Usurpation, and in RY 763 there are probably fewer than 100 of them left.<br /> <br /> Some educated mortals will have heard of Exigents, and thus the other Exalted I listed could in rare circumstances try to pass themselves off as Exigents. If they also know what those are. So some priests and exorcists will think of Exigents. Others will probably assume it's a spirit or god-blood.<br /> <br /> Can the average mortal trained as an Immaculate monk see through Arcane Fate fairly often? I dunno, but I think they (and the Exalted monks) ought to be able to -- either as an accidental or unavoidable side effect of their training, or as something the higher-up Dragon-Blooded deliberately added to their training that the Sidereals can abstain from teaching but can't effectively remove from the religion.<br /> <br /> Monks won't mistake them for a Lunar or Solar/Abyssal and call up a Wyld Hunt. I do think it'd be fitting for them to interpret Sidereals as potentially dangerous Exigents, god-bloods, or rogue spirits; distrust them; treat them somewhat poorly; and occasionally fight them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-25-2015, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T08:22:15-07:00","id":639110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=639098#post639098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect the average person doesn't know what an Exigent is, and lumps all Exigents, Sidereals, Getimians, Liminals, and Green Sun Princes into &quot;Weird glowy thing, probably a dangerous spirit, run away and find a priest/monk/exorcist.&quot; Exigents aren't a group with any unifying characteristics aside from their origins, they've been on the decline since the Usurpation, and in RY 763 there are probably fewer than 100 of them left.<br /> <br /> Some educated mortals will have heard of Exigents, and thus the other Exalted I listed could in rare circumstances try to pass themselves off as Exigents. If they also know what those are. So some priests and exorcists will think of Exigents. Others will probably assume it's a spirit or god-blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my favorite stories is when I ran a Lunars game, and the group, while traveling with a scholar, was accosted by some bandits with an earth elemental at their beck and call. The scholar botched his Occult roll, and thought that it was a Jade Lion, one of the guardians of the gates to the Underworld. The players didn't question it, didn't roll Occult of their own (and at least two out of the three probably would have succeeded), freaked out, ran away as fast as possible, leaving their wagon and stuff behind, and then proceeded to stalk the bandits for several days, waiting for them to go back to the underworld so the Lunars could block whatever the entrance was.<br /> <br /> I asked them later, and for some reason they thought that since the bandits had a 'Jade Lion' they thought that they were connected to an Abyssal in some way, if one of the bandits wasn't an Abyssal themselves. So basically, even educated mortals haven't heard of everything or can be as thick as a brick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1746-pants-o-doom","name":"Pants O Doom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T08:41:00-07:00","id":639127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=638714#post638714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 3.0, I expect...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kallipolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=638732#post638732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=638772#post638772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=639098#post639098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect...</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits generally look a little more inhuman than a typical Exalt, and usually <i>don't</i> glow fantastically when they use their powers.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say that the average peasant knows a great deal about the difference between spirits and the Exalted or between Exigents and Sidereals and such, but rather that some of y'all are expecting too much. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We know that the Immaculates teach the people to watch out for the signs of the Anathema (&quot;glows gold/sun symbols on forehead,&quot; &quot;glows silver/moon symbols on forehead&quot;), and that they teach the people to run and get them for big showy supernatural displays even when it's <i>not</i> categorically Anathema, so that a squad of monks can run in and <s>beat the shit out of it</s> assess the situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-25-2015, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T08:43:55-07:00","id":639128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=639127#post639127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(&quot;Run away and find an Immaculate/priest/DB&quot; is fair, though.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine in Exalted Modern, you'll have idiots that want to take a pictures/video with their smart phones. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T10:09:21-07:00","id":639261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=639128#post639128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine in Exalted Modern, you'll have idiots that want to take a pictures/video with their smart phones. </div> </div> </div> </div>Well, of course. How else are you going to earn Social Media Respect Points?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5492-xeno426","name":"Xeno426","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5492_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T00:18:05-07:00","id":639930,"title":"","content":"You know, it's entirely possible that Exigents don't have Caste Marks, like Dragonblood.<br /> After all, it's not like they have Castes.<br /> So the &quot;if you see a Caste Mark, it's a body-stealing immortal Yozi priest who stole power from the gods&quot; teaching might still apply.<br /> Also, it was mentioned that Exigents used to be very rare.<br /> Finally, peasants are not always good at nuance in religious doctrine (except where that nuance allows them to continue cultural practices or fight the power) so if they're told that 90% of the time, if you see a caste mark its an Anathema, but 10% of the time it's just a mortal who was given power from the Gods (which is extremely heretical anyway), they're probably still going to run off to find a monk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T00:31:57-07:00","id":639935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=639930#post639930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, it's entirely possible that Exigents don't have Caste Marks, like Dragonblood.</div> </div> </div> </div>With as varied a set of possibilities Exigents are supposed to allow, why definitively declare that none will ever have marks on their foreheads as part of their anima?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=639930#post639930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all, it's not like they have Castes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excepting of course for the ones that will - perhaps Ahlat is puissant enough to have more than one Exigent, and the two represent very different sides of him? Why not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=639930#post639930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the &quot;if you see a Caste Mark, it's a body-stealing immortal Yozi priest who stole power from the gods&quot; teaching might still apply.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might, but I don't think so. Hopefully we can get someone involved in the writing process here to answer the question one way or the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=639930#post639930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it was mentioned that Exigents used to be very rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are the Exalted themselves! They still have a tendency to bump into each other that crosses the line into straight-up uncanny. Hell, with only like a dozen Solar Exaltations, the Solars managed to make it into the Immaculate Texts. <br /> <br /> And even if the Sun <i>never</i> granted a new Exigence from the time he turned his face away to the time he turned it back, that might stop the one-and-dones, but it won't prevent the ones that manage to persist through reincarnation, bloodlines, or stranger means still!<br /> <br /> I mean, c'mon, man, one of the art previews had an Exigent kowtowing to the <i>Empress</i>. A peasant's gonna run and get a monk, not because &quot;probably Anathema,&quot; but because &quot;definitely supernatural.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-26-2015, 03:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T00:40:55-07:00","id":639937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, since people have asked quite a few times-- no, Exigents aren't Anathema. The Immaculate Order and its Sidereal architects aren't simpletons and in the bigger, wider setting of EX3, &quot;all non-DB Exalts&quot; isn't a workable Anathema definition. Exigents basically fall under the same heading as God-Blooded-- the result of improper congress between gods and mortals, and thus shameful and karmically banjaxed, but not the end of the world or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are likely less than 100 Exigents around when the Empress vanishes, maybe even significantly fewer than 50 across all of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Relevant quotes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-26-2015, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T09:43:07-07:00","id":640365,"title":"","content":"I think actually Exigents can have caste marks, or not, depending on the individual. Except their &quot;caste&quot; marks presumably would just be the sign of their patron god.<br /> Otherwise I agree with you Wizard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T10:11:16-07:00","id":640400,"title":"","content":"I wasn't saying they definitely won't. Just that they might not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T10:54:45-07:00","id":640434,"title":"","content":"There's still probably a decent non-zero chance a Dragon-Blood that is not very well-read in the Immaculate Texts could jump the gun and yell &quot;Anethema!&quot;, much to the derision of his peers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5492-xeno426","name":"Xeno426","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5492_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T11:05:28-07:00","id":640448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xeno426</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=640434#post640434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's still probably a decent non-zero chance a Dragon-Blood that is not very well-read in the Immaculate Texts could jump the gun and yell &quot;Anethema!&quot;, much to the derision of his peers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like all religions there are those who have a more liberal view of the Immaculate Text (I know it says that all Solars are Anathema, but my sister seems to be herself) and those who take the Immaculate Text too far (If it glows and isn't dragonblooded, kill it.) More common is the middle ground (Only Solars and Lunars are Anathema. Everything else should be treated with caution.)<br /> <br /> I suspect Dragonbloods on either extreme don't get very far in the Imperial Hierarchy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T11:09:08-07:00","id":640449,"title":"","content":"I'd think that in addition to Lookshy, other areas of Creation that retained Immaculate religion probably have their own local version, unless they've been a satrapy for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T11:16:34-07:00","id":640454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=640449#post640449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd think that in addition to Lookshy, other areas of Creation that retained Immaculate religion probably have their own local version, unless they've been a satrapy for a while.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My Twilight is a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cafeteria_Catholicism\" target=\"_blank\">Cafeteria Immaculate</a> (she doesn't talk about it as she knows it's kind of crazy for a Solar to keep that identity). She is from Lookshy, so their Immaculate Faith is less &quot;Kill all Anathema&quot; and more &quot;Try to follow the Immaculate Dragons as Role Models&quot;. I also have a homebrew Immaculate Sect based on<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/The-Madonna-115th-Street-Community/dp/0300042647\" target=\"_blank\"> the Madonna of 115th Street</a>. It is a Lookshy helot sect that actual worships the Immaculate Dragons as deities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T12:09:17-07:00","id":640503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=640448#post640448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like all religions there are those who have a more liberal view of the Immaculate Text (I know it says that all Solars are Anathema, but my sister seems to be herself) and those who take the Immaculate Text too far (If it glows and isn't dragonblooded, kill it.) More common is the middle ground (Only Solars and Lunars are Anathema. Everything else should be treated with caution.)<br /> <br /> I suspect Dragonbloods on either extreme don't get very far in the Imperial Hierarchy.</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression is that &quot;Anathema&quot; is becoming a formal clerical finding, much like &quot;excommunicable heresy&quot; is in a hierarchical church. The Solars and Lunars definitely are, no ifs ands or buts. Abyssals might have made it onto the &quot;definitely Anathema&quot; list by now, on account of their caste marks are the correct shape and all, they are just the wrong color. Other types of Exalted are on the &quot;get a priest&quot; list, and might be individually declared Anathema or not. There are undoubtedly Exigents who work for the Realm, and it does seem likely that a Sid caught in the anima-open might pretend to be one.<br /> <br /> For other categories of supernatural beings, I assume that Fair Folk are auto-Anathema, as are unbound demons, and gods might declared it on a case-by-case basis, but it's hard to tell if my brain is pulling this from the &quot;I read it somewhere&quot; bucket or the &quot;I made it up because it sounds plausible&quot; bucket.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T12:35:04-07:00","id":640556,"title":"","content":"I think the Devs declared that &quot;Anathema only includes Solars and Lunars. It no longer means 'anything we think is grody.' &quot; (paraphrased)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T12:44:08-07:00","id":640565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aretii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=640503#post640503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My impression is that &quot;Anathema&quot; is becoming a formal clerical finding, much like &quot;excommunicable heresy&quot; is in a hierarchical church. The Solars and Lunars definitely are, no ifs ands or buts. Abyssals might have made it onto the &quot;definitely Anathema&quot; list by now, on account of their caste marks are the correct shape and all, they are just the wrong color. Other types of Exalted are on the &quot;get a priest&quot; list, and might be individually declared Anathema or not. There are undoubtedly Exigents who work for the Realm, and it does seem likely that a Sid caught in the anima-open might pretend to be one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the idea of there being an inquisition Trial of Anathema, but I don't think many Solars and Lunars are going to sit around and let some Monk decide if they are anathema or not. <br /> <br /> That is probably why there is a line between Anathema and other dangerous Supernaturals. Anathema are kill on sight because their powers are so scary, there is no way a trail would be fair. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T12:47:53-07:00","id":640568,"title":"","content":"Actually, that was refuted by a Kickstarter update.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Immaculates apply the technical term Anathema\u2014in the Realm it\u2019s a formal clerical finding\u2014to anything that the order finds abhorrent to stable and prosperous life. Solar and Lunar Exalted are always Anathema; the label can also potentially encompass Fair Folk, beastmen, elementals, and demons who threaten Realm interests, as well as gods and their Exigent champions who\u2019ve gone into open rebellion against the Immaculate Philosophy.<br /> <br /> In practice, most inhabitants of the Realm (and Immaculate-influenced cultures in general) associate the term \u201cAnathema\u201d exclusively with the Solar and especially Lunar Exalted. The Lunar Anathema in particular are great fearsome terrors used by Realm peasants to frighten children into bed at night. Most individuals within the boundaries of the Realm are well-aware of the iconography of the Solar and Lunar Anathema\u2014their Caste brands, and the golden and argent hues of their auras\u2014the better to render assistance to the Wyld Hunt\u2019s investigators and trackers. On the subject of other sorts of \u201cAnathema,\u201d the common folk are left ignorant, lest they be tempted to worship something they don\u2019t understand\u2014it\u2019s enough for them to know that interaction with the supernatural is the responsibility of the Dragon-Blooded. Public duty when confronted with the unknown is to run and fetch a monk or Exalt. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T13:16:28-07:00","id":640588,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's what I was thinking of. I even remembered some of the language verbatim!<br /> <br /> Clearly I am cut out to be an Immaculate, not a peasant :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T14:25:49-07:00","id":640648,"title":"","content":"Uh well, huh. I probably even read that year(s?) ago, and forgot it.<br /> <br /> Well in that case it is totally legit for Sidereals to repeatedly get labelled Anathema and hunted at the least convenient moments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T14:45:15-07:00","id":640670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/626155-sidereals-and-children?p=640648#post640648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well in that case it is totally legit for Sidereals to repeatedly get labelled Anathema and hunted at the least convenient moments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you reading the same passage as me? <br /> <br /> A Siddie's only gonna get the A-word thrown at him when he's glowing gold or silver, or judged by a monk/DB to be acting against the DB hegemony. Note that it didn't say <i>all</i> Exigents were Anathema - <i>the only things</i> <b>categorically</b> stamped as such are Solars and Lunars!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-26-2015, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.the